FGA_CHECK:212-6.3-1	2026-11-18 20:27:15 UTC	GPT-6 Astra, ChatGPT Pro mode, this run	targeted proof check	For an action groupoid, the geometric fibre of (source,target) over (x,y), when nonempty, is a translate of the stabilizer of x. Consequently the finite-fibre condition forces zero-dimensional stabilizers, and finite-type zero-dimensional group schemes over a field are finite. Conversely finite stabilizers make every such geometric fibre finite. This verifies the practical restriction described in the remark. The question about removing it is historical, not asserted to remain open today.	212, p. 114, Remark 6.3(1)	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/FGA_CHECK_checkpoint_12_20261119T0612Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
FGA_CHECK:212-6.3-2-affine-example	2026-11-18 20:27:15 UTC	GPT-6 Astra, ChatGPT Pro mode, this run	independent re-proof	Own explicit example supporting the non-effectiveness warning: over a field of characteristic not two let X=A1 and R be the disjoint union of the diagonal A1 and the graph of t maps to -t restricted to Gm, inside X times X. The two branches are disjoint as subfunctors; inversion and composition give an equivalence relation. Its projections are etale and quasi-finite, with fibres of size two off zero and size one at zero, and are not finite. Any morphism h:X to a prescheme that equalizes R is invariant under t maps to -t everywhere: equality holds off zero, and near zero both maps land in a common affine neighbourhood of their common value, where equality follows from schematic density. Thus its coequalizer is the usual finite-group quotient q:t maps to t^2, by the affine finite quotient result 5.1. But X times_q X is Spec k[x,y]/(x^2-y^2); at the origin it has the two branches and is not the diagonal neighbourhood appearing in R. Therefore R is not effective in preschemes. This verifies an independent affine example, not the specific Nagata construction mentioned in the print.	212, p. 114, Remark 6.3(2)	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/FGA_CHECK_checkpoint_12_20261119T0612Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
