FGA_CHECK:212-7.1-closure	2026-11-18 20:27:15 UTC	GPT-6 Astra, ChatGPT Pro mode, this run	independent re-proof	Let C be the schematic closure of C prime in A over the DVR V. Affine-locally its coordinate ring injects into the localization defining C prime, hence is torsion-free over V and therefore flat. Its generic fibre is C prime. Products of these flat V-schemes are flat and have schematically dense generic fibre. Multiplication and inversion preserve C on the generic fibre; the defining ideal therefore pulls back to zero on C times C and C, respectively, by that schematic density. The identity section likewise factors through C. Thus C is a flat closed subgroup scheme; it is proper since A is proper. With projectivity of the abelian scheme over this DVR as a separate background input, the translation equivalence relation C times A on A meets 6.1. This verifies the closure step, not all remaining abelian-scheme assertions on the next page.	212, p. 114, proof of Proposition 7.1	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/FGA_CHECK_checkpoint_12_20261119T0612Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
