FGA_CHECK:236-4-conic-example	2026-11-19 04:06:23 UTC	GPT-6 Astra, ChatGPT Pro mode, this run	targeted proof check	For the projective flat conic xy=t z^2, the special fibre is two projective lines meeting in one node. Line bundles of multidegree (a,d-a) exist for every integer a and have the same Hilbert polynomial 2n+d+1 for the plane polarization. Their Picard identity component is trivial, so they give infinitely many discrete special-fibre points with that fixed polynomial. Hence the corresponding fixed-polynomial locus is not quasi-compact and cannot be of finite type over the base. The general Hilbert-polynomial open-and-closed decomposition uses the already stated flat-family invariance.	236, p. 241, opening of section 4	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/FGA_CHECK_checkpoint_12_20261119T0612Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
