FGA_CHECK:236-4.1-a-b	2026-11-19 04:08:24 UTC	GPT-6 Astra, ChatGPT Pro mode, this run	targeted proof check	The subset E, not the polynomial Q, is the object whose quasi-compactness is asserted in a. For a locally finite-type scheme over Noetherian S, a quasi-compact subset lies in a finite union of affine finite-type opens; conversely every subset of such a Noetherian open is quasi-compact. Since Hilbert-polynomial strata are open and closed, a quasi-compact E meets only finitely many, proving a implies b. A finite set of polynomials has a finite set of coefficients, proving b implies b prime where the indicated coefficients are defined. The substantive reverse boundedness implications and identification with a bounded family require the announced theorem and local universal families; they remain background pending the rest of the statement. For n below two, negative-index coefficients require the conventional value zero rather than a new coefficient.	236, p. 242, theorem 4.1, data and conditions a, b, b prime	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/FGA_CHECK_checkpoint_12_20261119T0612Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
