ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.1.1.6-p5-reindexing-base	2026-11-18 13:41:23 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted proof check	For a fibered functor p:E->B and f:S->T, the cartesian universal property identifies morphisms X->Y above f with morphisms X->f*Y in the S-fiber. Dually, cocartesian lifting identifies them with f_*X->Y in the T-fiber. Hence the two arrows corresponding to u0,u1 use the common base f, not the total-category arrows u0,u1 as transport indices. This checks the four type corrections, not the full homotopy-lifting assertion or the external Giraud citation.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.1.2.1-p7-total-differential	2026-11-18 13:50:11 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted proof check	On L^{p1,...,pn}, the j-th signed summand is (-1)^{p1+...+p(j-1)}d_j. It raises total degree by one, so its sum is the differential on integral L. For i<j, applying d_i changes the sign attached to d_j once, whereas applying d_j does not change the sign attached to d_i; commuting d_i,d_j therefore cancel in cross terms and d_j^2=0 kills the diagonal terms. This checks typing and d^2=0 wherever the indicated direct sums exist; it does not prove their existence in an arbitrary additive category.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
