ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.1.4.7-truncation-adjunction-and-cohomology	2026-11-18 14:38:19 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted proof check	For Y zero below n, the degree-n component of a chain map X->Y kills Im d_X^(n-1), hence uniquely factors through X^n/Im d_X^(n-1). This gives Hom(t_[n X,Y)->Hom(X,Y) in the printed direction. For Z zero above n, a chain map Z->X lands in Ker d_X^n at degree n, yielding the printed Hom(Z,t_n]X)->Hom(Z,X). At the boundary degree, both truncations have Ker d^n/Im d^(n-1); on retained degrees their cohomology equals that of X and on deleted degrees it is zero. These calculations prove the stated cohomology bounds and both quasi-isomorphism composites for L in C^n] and M in C^[n.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
