ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.2.3.3-localization-proof	2026-11-18 16:19:11 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted proof and type check	Let Q:A->A(H^{-1}). Since s^0 is a homotopy equivalence, Q(s^0) is invertible. Both Q(d^0) and Q(d^1) are its inverse, using s^0 d^i=Id. Thus Q(ud^0)=Q(ud^1), so Q identifies elementary homotopic maps and hence all homotopic maps. It factors through B=Hotsimpl(T). Conversely A->B inverts H, yielding A(H^{-1})->B. The two resulting functors are inverse on objects and morphisms by their defining factorizations. Surjectivity can also be checked directly: every inverse of an h in a localization word is represented, after passing to B, by a chosen homotopy inverse of h. This validates the printed proof up to its open parenthesis; the dual proof continuation remains on the next page.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
