ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.1.1.0-internal-Hom-degrees	2026-11-18 17:09:49 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted proof and type check	For U in T, sections over U of degree n of internal Homs_A(E,F) are A|U-linear simplicial maps from the free integral simplicial module Z^(Delta(n)) tensor_Z E|U to F|U. The A action is on the E factor. This follows from the exponential description in (2.3.1) and the free-module adjunction for the representable simplicial parameter Delta(n). The right-hand Hom is therefore a sheaf on T, whereas the left-hand internal Homs is an object of Simpl(T) before evaluation at degree n. The A indices are legitimately implicit by the printed preceding convention.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.1.1.1-3-tensor-Hom-and-global-sections	2026-11-18 17:09:49 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted proof and type check	The convention on p55 makes A commutative. Currying an A-bilinear map L times M to N identifies internal Homs_A(L tensor_A M,N) with internal Homs_A(L,internal Homs_A(M,N)); this is an isomorphism of A-module objects in Simpl(T). Applying global sections of T degree by degree gives an isomorphism of simplicial sets: both outer Homs in (3.1.1.2) must be plain, while the inner Homs remains the internal A-module object. Taking degree zero of that simplicial set gives ordinary A-linear simplicial morphisms and hence (3.1.1.3). Equivalently, a global section in Simpl(T) is determined by its degree-zero element, with higher components given by degeneracies. No commutation of global sections with pi_0 is used. The supplied outer underlines in (3.1.1.2) are transcription errors, not defects in the original.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
