ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.3.6-special-module-proof	2026-11-18 19:37:45 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted special-module and resolution proof	Write M=A tensor_Z P with P degreewise flat and H_*(P) graded flat over Z. Then L tensor_A M is canonically L tensor_Z P. Shuffle associativity gives the displayed commutative square. Kunneth and Eilenberg-Zilber identify H_*(C) tensor_Z H_*(P) with H_*(C tensor_Z P), for C=A and C=L: flat P computes the derived tensor, and flat H_*(P) kills the higher Tor terms. The left arrow is obtained by tensoring the C=A isomorphism with H_*(L) over H_*(A), which preserves an isomorphism without assuming H_*(L) flat. The bottom arrow is the canonical associativity/unit isomorphism. Therefore the upper arrow is an isomorphism.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.3.7-graded-flatness-proof	2026-11-18 19:37:45 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted special-module and resolution proof	For special M=A tensor_Z P, the preceding canonical isomorphism identifies H_*(M) with H_*(A) tensor_Z H_*(P). Tensoring any graded H_*(A)-module with this module is tensoring its underlying graded Z-module with H_*(P). Each degree is a direct sum of tensors with flat Z-modules H_j(P), so this operation is exact. Thus H_*(M) is flat as a graded H_*(A)-module.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.3.8-resolution-reduction	2026-11-18 19:37:45 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	targeted special-module and resolution proof	Assuming a functorial epimorphism L_0(M)->M with special source and a surjection on all homology groups, put K_1=ker(L_0(M)->M) and iterate the same construction on K_1, then on its successive kernels. The homology long exact sequence has zero connecting maps because the preceding maps onto H_n(M) are surjective in every n. It consequently yields short exact sequences 0->H_n(K_1)->H_n(L_0(M))->H_n(M)->0, and the same at each successive step. Splicing gives both the functorial augmented chain resolution and the required resolution after H_*. The actual construction of L_0 begins here but continues on p89; that continuation is not yet certified.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.3.8-functorial-special-epimorphism	2026-11-18 19:43:08 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	explicit resolution, spectral-sequence proof and counterexample	An explicit construction verifies the asserted Z case without consulting the cited external text. For the nonnegative normalized complex C of M, let P be the direct sum over n>=0 of sphere complexes S^n Z^(Z_n C), together with disks D^n Z^(C_n) for n>=1. Map a sphere generator to its indicated cycle; map the top disk generator to its indicated element and its bottom generator to that element's differential. This is functorial, degreewise surjective (the disks cover positive degrees and the degree-zero sphere covers C_0), and surjective on homology. Every term is flat and each homology sheaf is a free Z-module sheaf from the sphere summands. Dold-Kan sends P to a special simplicial Z-module and preserves these properties. For general A, put L_0(M)=A tensor_Z P. The composite to M is surjective on underlying simplicial modules and on homology because the surjections P->M and H(P)->H(M) factor through it via the unit of A. Thus the kernel iteration proved on p88 supplies the functorial resolution.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.3.2-direct-graded-Tor-proof	2026-11-18 19:43:08 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	explicit resolution, spectral-sequence proof and counterexample	The vertical chain resolution L_.(F) is exact and has special, hence degreewise A-flat, horizontal simplicial modules. Applying vertical Dold-Kan forms finite direct sums in each vertical degree, preserving specialness and the homology resolution. The resulting diagonal is a flat simplicial A-module quasi-isomorphic to F: the first-quadrant comparison spectral sequence and Eilenberg-Zilber identify its homology with that of F. Therefore Delta(E tensor_A L)=E tensor_A Delta L computes E derived-tensor_ell F directly, without relying on the disputed D_hv factorization. Take horizontal homology first. Lemma3.3.3.6 identifies the q-th group in resolution degree p with k_q(H_*(E) tensor_{H_*(A)} H_*(L_p(F))). By3.3.3.7-8, H_*(L_.(F)) is a flat graded resolution of H_*(F). Vertical homology therefore gives k_q Tor_p^{H_*(A)}(H_*(E),H_*(F)), and first-quadrant convergence gives the claimed abutment. Functorial constructions give naturality.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
