ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.3.9bc-constant-case-and-Postnikov-check	2026-11-18 19:43:08 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	explicit resolution, spectral-sequence proof and counterexample	For constant A, the direct normalization/Eilenberg-Zilber comparison from3.3.2.8 identifies these constructions with the usual nonnegative chain-complex tensor spectral sequences. For(c), use the functorial Postnikov tower of E as an A-module. Its successive layer is H_q(E)[q], with the A-action on H_q(E) through A->H_0(A). Apply the exact derived tensor with F to the tower. The associated Postnikov exact couple, indexed with its initial page E2, has E2_{p,q}=H_p(H_q(E) derived-tensor_A F), with differential bidegree(-r,r-1). Connectivity of F and of each layer gives p,q>=0; for each total degree only finitely many layers contribute, yielding convergence to H_*(E derived-tensor_A F). The maps are H_0(A)-linear and functorial. This checks the displayed claim by the Postnikov construction; no consultation or verification of the external Quillen reference is claimed.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
