ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.4.3-chi-square	2026-11-18 19:56:36 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	derived adjunction, triangle naturality and type proof	The true-triangle functor from p90 is induced by applying extension of scalars to a flat representative arrow and its cone. Chi then reads off exactly that cone triangle in D(B). Applying chi first gives the original cone triangle, and the exact ell-derived tensor takes it to the same base-changed cone triangle. Thus the square commutes naturally. The unlabeled right vertical arrow is the corresponding chi for B; the original labels only the A-side vertical arrow.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.4.4-derived-adjunction-proof	2026-11-18 19:56:36 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	derived adjunction, triangle naturality and type proof	Let Q(E)->E be a functorial flat simplicial resolution, L(E)=B tensor_A Q(E), and U the restriction functor, which preserves quasi-isomorphisms. Define the derived unit by E <- Q(E) -> U(B tensor_A Q(E)), using the unit A->B, and define the counit L(UF)=B tensor_A Q(UF)->B tensor_A UF->F by the B-action. Naturality follows from Q. The two triangle identities reduce on flat representatives to the ordinary tensor/restriction unit and multiplication identities; the resolution comparisons become isomorphisms after L because tensor preserves quasi-isomorphisms between flat modules. Hence Hom_D(B)(L(E),F) is naturally Hom_D(A)(E,UF). For n>=0 apply this to sigma^n F; for n<0 apply it to sigma^(-n) E and use L(sigma E)=sigma L(E). This proves every stated Ext degree using only nonnegative suspensions. It also justifies the printed localization passage without assuming that B-module right denominators are automatically cofinal among all A-module denominators. No flatness of B over A is required.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.4.5-exact-sequences-and-prime	2026-11-18 19:56:36 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	derived adjunction, triangle naturality and type proof	For a distinguished triangle of B-modules, exact restriction produces a distinguished triangle of A-modules. Naturality of the derived adjunction in F and its compatibility with suspension make the comparison commute with all maps, including the connecting map, in the associated long exact Ext sequences. This proves the displayed two downward comparisons and their continuation. In the E-variable, exactness of L and contravariance of Ext give the analogous statement for a distinguished triangle of A-modules. Such a triangle E-prime->E->E-double-prime must terminate at sigma E-prime, which proves the necessary final-prime repair. The original D(A) in the F-variable is likewise ill-typed for Ext_B and must be D(B).		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.4.6-equivalence-proof	2026-11-18 20:04:24 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	flat-resolution and adjunction proof	For a quasi-isomorphism A->B and a flat A-module E, the derived unit E->U(B tensor^ell_A E) is represented by E tensor_A(A->B), a quasi-isomorphism by the actual lemma numbered 3.3.2.1 on p85. Replacing an arbitrary E by a flat resolution proves the unit is invertible for every object. Restriction U preserves and detects homology and is conservative on the derived categories: the underlying cone is acyclic exactly when the B-module cone is acyclic. The adjunction triangle identity U(epsilon_F) composed with eta_(UF)=Id and invertibility of eta imply U(epsilon_F) is invertible; conservativity makes epsilon_F invertible. Thus the stated functors are quasi-inverse. This proof uses the directly constructed ell-derived adjunction and does not require the unresolved hv descent.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.4.7-transitivity-proof	2026-11-18 20:04:24 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	flat-resolution and adjunction proof	Choose a flat A-module resolution QF->F. The B-module B tensor_A QF is flat degreewise: for every degree n and B_n-module N, N tensor_(B_n)(B_n tensor_(A_n) QF_n) identifies with N tensor_(A_n) QF_n, an exact functor of N. It can therefore represent the argument of C tensor^ell_B without further derivation. Ordinary associativity gives C tensor_B(B tensor_A QF) = C tensor_A QF, which represents C tensor^ell_A F. The identification is canonical and natural in F and in the ring maps, and requires no flatness assumption on B over A. The three printed script-ell superscripts and headed isomorphism have the required types.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.5.1-diagonal-free-algebra-resolution	2026-11-18 20:07:21 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	free resolution, cofinality and tensor proof	The standard augmented free-algebra resolution is degreewise a resolution of B in its resolution direction: the underlying augmented simplicial object has the standard splitting. Its underlying bisimplicial abelian-group homology therefore has only the augmented row. The first-quadrant spectral sequence and Eilenberg-Zilber identify the homology of its diagonal with that of B. In diagonal degree n its term is a free A_n-algebra, hence flat as an A_n-module by the already established free-algebra construction. Thus Delta P_A(B)->B is an A-algebra quasi-isomorphism with flat underlying A-module. The author-defined diagonal-subobject terminology is retained.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.3.3.5.2-algebra-derived-tensor-proof	2026-11-18 20:07:21 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	free resolution, cofinality and tensor proof	The right fraction calculus of 3.1.8(ii) gives the filtered denominator categories in the footnote; taking the pair for B and C preserves filtering. Any denominator algebra P->B can be refined by Delta P_A(P)->P->B, so flat denominators form a cofinal subsystem; common refinements and equalizations can be refined in the same way. For flat P,Q, every transition in P tensor_A Q induced by a quasi-isomorphism of either flat denominator is a quasi-isomorphism by lemma 3.3.2.1 applied to underlying A-modules. The flat-denominator pro-object is consequently essentially constant. If P is flat, P tensor_A Q->P tensor_A C is a quasi-isomorphism; symmetrically for flat Q. These identify the stated values in D(A-Alg). The universal pro-object definition of left derivation, as in 1.4.4 and the directly verified 3.3.2.6, then gives the asserted functor. This uses no unresolved hv-localization descent.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.4.1.1-boundary-bicomplex-proof	2026-11-18 20:10:33 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	bicomplex identities, totalization and full-faithfulness proof	For a cochain complex L, set (iL)^(p,0)=L^p for p<=0 and (iL)^(0,q)=L^q for q>=0, with the shared origin L^0 counted once and all interior terms zero. The horizontal and vertical boundary differentials are those of L. The only mixed square with two potentially nonzero successive boundary maps has composite d^0 d^(-1)=0, equal to the other composite through zero; hence this is a bicomplex under the printed commuting convention. Each total degree contains exactly one nonzero term, so either direct-sum or product totalization exists here and has term L^n. The signed simple-complex convention gives the original differential: the horizontal axis has q=0 and the vertical axis has p=0. A morphism iL->iM consists exactly of maps L^n->M^n commuting with every boundary differential, hence exactly a cochain map. This proves full faithfulness and the stated uniqueness from the associated simple complex, which must be L rather than the original unintroduced E. The one-axis embeddings of the nonpositive and nonnegative complex categories are the corresponding restrictions. No proof of the later announced derived retraction is claimed on this introductory page.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
