ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.4.1.3.5-Deligne-homotopy	2026-11-18 20:32:43 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	support and homotopy proofs; explicit reduced-functor and double-dual counterexamples	Define h-plus to be h in degrees >0 and zero in degrees <=0, and h-minus=h-h-plus. Put w=u+d h-plus+h-plus d. Since d squared is zero, w is a cochain map and v-w=d h-minus+h-minus d. On the axis bicomplexes h-plus gives a vertical cochain homotopy between iu and iw, and h-minus a horizontal one between iw and iv; compatibility with the transverse differential at the corner follows from d squared=0 and the stated zero parts. By the already audited 1.3.4, K carries these to cosimplicial and simplicial homotopies. Such homotopies are identities among component maps, preserved by any functor F. Normalization returns the corresponding vertical/horizontal bicomplex homotopies. With total differential d_h+(-1)^p d_v, the vertical homotopy receives the factor (-1)^p and the horizontal one is unchanged; the transverse terms cancel. Their sum is a total homotopy from Fu to Fv whenever the required total complexes exist. No unconditional existence claim beyond I-Q009 is made.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
