ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.4.2.2.1-contractible-quotient	2026-11-18 20:55:42 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	homotopy formulas, filtered-colimit proof and flat-resolution construction	Pullback of the degreewise-split extension along Z_i->Z preserves its graded splitting. In such a splitting write d_Y=(d_X,a;0,d_Z), so d_X a+a d_Z=0. If h contracts Z_i, set b=a h. Then d_X b-b d_Z=-a(d_Z h+h d_Z)=-a, so s(z)=(bz,z) is a chain section of the quotient. The chain retraction r(x,z)=x-bz has r u_i=Id, and Id-u_i r=s q is null-homotopic by s h q. Thus u_i is a homotopy equivalence. The extension F preserves homotopies by4.1.3.5, giving a homotopy equivalence F(u_i). This establishes the later-reference correction and uses no additivity or reducedness assumption on F.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
