ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:I.4.2.2.6-exponential-decomposition-and-sign	2026-11-18 21:16:36 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE second pass 2026-11-18	universal-property, sign, cross-effect and flatness proofs	For G=S, exterior algebra, or Gamma, the inclusions of E and F into E direct-sum F induce G(E) tensor G(F)->G(E direct-sum F); conversely the degree-one maps into the two tensor factors give the inverse by the relevant universal property. On generators the composites are identities, hence the graded-algebra maps are inverse. For exterior algebras, moving x-prime of degreeq past y of degreep gives exactly(-1)^(pq), so(x tensor y)(x-prime tensor y-prime)=(-1)^(pq)xx-prime tensor yy-prime. This multiplication remains strictly anticommutative: an odd pure tensor has an odd factor whose square is zero, and cross terms in the square of any odd sum cancel using anticommutativity, including in characteristic2. Thus the sign and the extra odd-square clause in note1 are both necessary and correctly stated.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
