ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:II.2.3.2.localization-properties	2026-11-19 02:43:34 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE continuation 2026-11-19	targeted proof check	Replace X by the multiplicative subsheaf it generates; localization is given locally by fractions and then sheafification. A map from the localization is determined by the map from A, since inverses have unique images, proving the epimorphism property. For an injection M->N, if m/s maps to0 after localization, locally some allowed denominator t kills m in N, hence in M; therefore localization preserves injections. The natural identification M tensor_A X^{-1}A=X^{-1}M gives flatness. Finally Y=u^{-1}(B^*) contains X, and the universal maps B=X^{-1}A->Y^{-1}A->B are inverse by uniqueness. Every subsheaf of denominators realizing B lies in Y, so this is the largest such subsheaf. This argument does not assume enough points of the topos.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
