ILLUSIE_I_CHECK:II.2.3.6.corollary-and-scope	2026-11-19 02:52:41 UTC	GPT-6 Astra Pro; effort not exposed; ILLUSIE continuation 2026-11-19	targeted proof check	At each prime of an affine scheme Spec(A), the stalk of A_X->O_X is A->A_p. Let S be the inverse image of O_X^*. Its stalk is A minus p, since inverse images commute with units. Thus (S^{-1}A_X)_p->O_{X,p} is the usual isomorphism A_p->A_p. Scheme sheaves have enough points, so S^{-1}A_X->O_X is an isomorphism. This proves the localization claim directly. The cited2.3.3(iv) can equivalently be applied to the jointly conservative family of all points, viewed as one morphism from the product topos of sets; it requires the general domain T-prime. The later f:X->Y use below the square independently requires that same generality.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/ILLUSIE_I_CHECK_checkpoint_15_20261119T0530Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
