TOHOKU_CHECK:TOH-p206-fixed-locus-closedness-refined	2026-11-18 22:39:36 UTC	GPT-6 Astra; ChatGPT Pro; effort not exposed; TOHOKU second pass	targeted proof check	Refined statement: require the fixed-point set to be closed, for example by assuming X Hausdorff. For each g its fixed set is the inverse image of the closed diagonal under x maps to (x,gx); intersections are closed. For a finite prime-order group the nonfree locus is this fixed set. Its invariant closed image in the orbit quotient is closed by the quotient topology.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/TOHOKU_CHECK_final_20261118T2340Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.before-note-bindings.tsv	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/TOHOKU_CHECK_final_20261118T2340Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv
TOHOKU_CHECK:p215:5.6.1:correct-factor	2026-11-18 22:39:36 UTC	GPT-6 Astra; ChatGPT Pro; effort not exposed; TOHOKU second pass	independent re-proof	Refined statement: if B is constructed as the product of point-supported sheaves with chosen modules B_x, the factors for internal Hom(A,B) are Hom_(O(x))(A(x),B_x). The point-stalk/right-adjoint Hom identity and preservation of products by Hom give this formula. The full stalk B(x) is not the chosen factor B_x; the Sierpinski calculation in p215:5.6.1:factor-versus-stalk verifies the distinction.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/TOHOKU_CHECK_final_20261118T2340Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.before-note-bindings.tsv	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/TOHOKU_CHECK_final_20261118T2340Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv
