VERDIER_CHECK:I.1.4.3.5:first-formula	2026-11-18 14:09:22 UTC	GPT-6 Astra (ChatGPT Pro mode); effort not exposed; run 2026-11-18	targeted proof check	The printed factor order is retained. In this extension ker(f) has order two, so conjugation fixes its unique nonidentity element and the kernel is central. The displayed a=s(sigma2)s(sigma1 sigma2)^(-1)s(sigma1) lies in ker(f); conjugating a by s(sigma1) gives s(sigma1)s(sigma2)s(sigma1 sigma2)^(-1)=a. This checks the factor order only, not the full cocycle identity.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_02_20261118T1434Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_05_20261118T1811Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv; french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_06_20261118T1905Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv
VERDIER_CHECK:I.1.3.9.1–2	2026-11-18 14:19:28 UTC	GPT-6 Astra (ChatGPT Pro mode); effort not exposed; run 2026-11-18	used and rechecked in this run	Rechecked the opposite-action definitions while deciding p. 50: inversion i:G-circle to G satisfies i(g perpendicular h)=i(g)i(h); T-circle(g)=T(g inverse)-op and c-circle(g,h) is the opposite of c(g inverse,h inverse) inverse. This is the exact identification used in the p. 50 cocycle check.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_02_20261118T1434Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_05_20261118T1811Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv; french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_06_20261118T1905Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv
VERDIER_CHECK:I.1.4.8:opposite-cocycle	2026-11-18 14:19:28 UTC	GPT-6 Astra (ChatGPT Pro mode); effort not exposed; run 2026-11-18	targeted proof check	The printed order alpha-circle(g,h)=alpha(g inverse,h inverse) inverse is retained. Put D(u)=(u inverse)-op for a natural isomorphism u. Then D(vu)=D(v)D(u), D respects whiskering by opposite functors, and D(epsilon u)=epsilon inverse D(u). Applying D to the compatibility diagram 1.4.3.11 at a=g inverse,b=h inverse, with the inversion homomorphism G-circle to G, produces precisely the opposite diagram with this scalar. The supplied source had transposed a,b. This checks the opposite scalar and its order.		french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_02_20261118T1434Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_05_20261118T1811Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv; french_school_pro_checks_20261117_work/returns/VERDIER_CHECK_checkpoint_06_20261118T1905Z_unzipped/VERDIER_CHECK/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv
