maps:src:F.4.1	2026-11-20	Claude Opus 5.5 at effort max (session setting), fork session c0f5e6ff of main session 4656fb33, Hexagon deposit preparation of S6_SERIES_GRIND cp10 Paper V	targeted proof check	[recorded on: maps:src:F.4.1 (02OC), steps 5-6; series:V:D (03KU)] holds: Theorem 7.2 step 5 (Wall's classification via the extended form, Conway et al. Thm 3.7(1)) gives M = N # Sigma for a homotopy 8-sphere Sigma; step 6 applies Kramer-Stolz, J. Differential Geom. 77 (2007) 177-188, Theorem A, p. 178, opened and read: a smooth simply connected 2m-manifold, 2m != 4, with integral homology Z+Z+Z satisfies M # Sigma = M for every homotopy sphere Sigma; HP^2 meets the hypotheses, so N # Sigma = N and the diffeomorphism is orientation-preserving as argued. Step 2's reflection R = I - v(v^t Q) was recomputed exactly: R^2 = I, R^t Q R = Q, v^t Q v = 2. Steps 3-4 (clutching coordinates) were read against the standard description of pi_3(SO(4)); not re-derived in full.	literature/kramer_stolz_2007/kramer_stolz_JDG77_2007.pdf (Zeta-Function-Foundation); S6_HEXAGON_DEPOSITS_20261120/V	s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/reviews/INTAKE_S6_SERIES_GRIND_cp10_20261120_CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
