series:V:C	2026-11-20	Claude Opus 5.5 at effort max (session setting), session aacf1302, which continues the fork c0f5e6ff after the account switch; re-check of the fork's checks at the user's request	independent re-proof	[recorded on: series:V:C (03KT); night:P1.8] holds for the printed formulas re-derived: the discriminant l^15(3125 l + 256) (sympy); the node at l0 = -256/3125, x0 = 64/625, is ordinary (f'' != 0), on a smooth total space (df/dl != 0) and irreducible (normalization genus 1); stable reduction gives Y^2 = X^5 + X + l^(1/4) at 0 and Y^2 = X^5 + m^(1/5) X + 1 at infinity, hence root orders 8 and 5; dx/y and x dx/y have divisors (6/5)[inf] - (9/8)[0] and (2/5)[inf] - (3/8)[0], so H = T^3 + T with T = O((2/5)[inf] - (3/8)[0]), deg H = 1/10, which Mumford's 10 lambda = delta_0 + 2 delta_1 confirms. Not covered: the rest of Theorem C, and P1.8's base-coordinate transport, which the run was still checking at cp10.	S6_HEXAGON_DEPOSITS_20261120/V/RECHECK_V_aacf1302_20261120.py (output .out)	s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/reviews/INTAKE_S6_SERIES_GRIND_cp10_20261120_CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
