maps:src:F.4.1	2026-11-20	Claude Opus 5.5 at effort max (session setting), session aacf1302, which continues the fork c0f5e6ff after the account switch; re-check of the fork's checks at the user's request	targeted proof check	[recorded on: V.7.2 (02OC) steps 2-6; maps:src:F.4.1; series:V:D (03KU)] holds: step 2's R = I - v(v^t Q) is the printed matrix, R^2 = I, R^t Q R = Q, and the printed descent carries every characteristic norm-2 vector of I_{3,1} with |d| < 120 (9,408 vectors, at most 59 reflections) to (1,1,1,1) by an integral isometry; steps 3-4 re-derived by hand: (e, p1/2) = (a - b, a + b), TS^4 = (1, -1), the HP^1 normal bundle = (1, 0), integrality of the normal coordinates = p characteristic, stable class a + b; step 5: Conway, Crowley, Powell and Sixt, author version v3 (Oct 2021), Definition 3.6 and Theorem 3.7(1), pp. 12-14, opened and read: equivalent smooth extended symmetric forms (H_4, lambda, S_M) give an orientation-preserving almost diffeomorphism, and their proof shows (lambda(x,x), S_M(x)) determines the unstable normal class, which is step 4's use; step 6: Kramer and Stolz, JDG 77 (2007), Theorem A, p. 178, opened and read; HP^2 meets its hypotheses; the orientation argument (degree +1 from x^2 = u) holds.	S6_HEXAGON_DEPOSITS_20261120/V/RECHECK_V_aacf1302_20261120.py (output .out)	s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/reviews/INTAKE_S6_SERIES_GRIND_cp10_20261120_CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
