cdp:st:D.1.13	2026-11-18T04:50:08.441928+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved counterexample; rejected printed surjectivity and positivity remain refuted Full canonical-line, relative-duality and coherent-splitting argument on the actual Wang fillings. Re-derived the M× canonical map ωS↦ωS∧dlogv and its invariance under the actual −6P lift. The unimodular rank-one map (z,v)↦(v,v²/z) converts the degenerating vector to a primitive unit vector; dq∧dlogu=−du∧dv at uv=q gives the extension. At the rank-two chart, q=z0z1z2 and the unimodular character determinant give q∏dlogzi=∏dzi. At infinity, s=r³, x_s=r⁴X, y_s=r⁶Y gives ds∧dx_s/y_s=3dr∧dX/Y; the order3 deck weights multiply to one, and the actual line-coordinate rescaling v′=r²v adds only a dr term to dlogv. The affine logarithmic translation likewise preserves the form, so KY=f*O(−1) holds through every filling. Flat Gorenstein relative duality and the actual D1.12 cup/base-change isomorphism give R²=detR¹=O(−1). D1.9’s nonzero full-fibre coefficient section is a subbundle O; Ext¹(O(−1),O)=H¹O(1)=0 splits R¹. Leray gives(1,1,0,0), with restriction rank1 on each smooth torus. The integral source topology was rechecked in D1.6. A dominating divisor would restrict to a nonzero effective topologically trivial divisor on a Kahler fibre, impossible by its positive intersection; this gives the actual meromorphic descent to P1 and a=1. Any biholomorphism to the sphere member would induce an H2 isomorphism, contradicting Z/2 versus0. New derivation after reading the supplied proof; not a blind review and not an independent human check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
