cdp:st:E8	2026-11-18	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	used and rechecked in this run	Source DLMFTheta2026; opened locus: NIST DLMF version1.2.8: equations20.2.1-2,20.2.6,20.2.12; 20.4.3-5 and20.4.8;20.5.1;20.7.5;20.13.1;23.3.9;23.6.1-2 and23.6.8-9;23.17.8. Opened every listed exact equation on the primary NIST pages, including its displayed nome and period conventions. The receiving conversion is vartheta_j(z,tau)=theta_j(pi*z|tau) and 2omega1=1,2omega3=tau. Under this conversion the heat coefficient is 1/(4pi*i) and the half-period value is pi^2(theta3^4+theta4^4)/3. Differentiating the locally normally convergent products yields eta'/eta and the Laurent coefficient of the logarithmic theta derivative; the proof explicitly gives this conversion and the elliptic principal-part comparison. This bounded formula-source reading does not claim a reading of the books cited by DLMF. Source-opening record only; no additional whole-proof review is inferred.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
cdp:st:E8	2026-11-18	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	Full theta determinant proof rederived. Adjoining(mu,beta/6) gives an exact index-six lattice enlargement and the identity-induced degree-six isogeny, preserving Kodaira–Spencer rank. Heat equation, eta derivative and h_mu=-wp-pi^2E2/3 cancel the E2 terms; differentiating wp(mu)=0 gives determinant -g2^2/(36pi^2g3). Checked root orders1 and2, the resulting determinant order2 at the order-three point, cancellation at the order-four point, and the nondegenerate cusp logarithmic diagonal.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
