maps:src:B.1.2	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: {""reader"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""full_receiving_proof_read"": true, ""current_check_event_ids"": [""new-maps-homotopy-read-20261117"", ""new-maps-B-homotopy-source-closure-20261117"", ""new-maps-final-small-program-20261117:maps_exact.py""], ""receiving_read_records"": [{""event_id"": ""new-maps-homotopy-read-20261117"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Full arguments read and rederived: stable framing, degree-twelve weighted Hopf factor, retained-angle Arf class, angle-forgotten cone nullhomotopy and conical wedge.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-B-homotopy-source-closure-20261117"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Closed the exact Bott, real APS, and Toda primary-source gates after the previously recorded full receiving-proof reads.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-final-small-program-20261117:maps_exact.py"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Full F2^4 invariant-covector enumeration, integral invariant lattices, actual named-family comparison matrices, exact symbolic lens arithmetic, and the flat Pauli symbol. This does not replace the stable-framing or APS geometric argument.""}], ""source_dependency_status"": ""Closed in the exact operative scopes recorded; provider citation/program reviews remain separately itemized rather than inferred from receiving reads."", ""exact_source_check_records"": [{""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_and_weight_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsAPS2"", ""opened_locators"": [""Section4, equations(4.11)–(4.14), printed pp.422–424; searchable text774–893"", ""Theorem(4.14), printed p.423 (PDF p.19), original formula visually checked""], ""scope"": ""For a parallelism on a (4k-1)-manifold the original real Adams invariant is epsilon(k) times the reduced Dirac eta invariant minus its connection transgression. The exact coefficient is epsilon(k)=1/2 for k odd. On the flat Lie-framed T3, k=1, the connection term is zero, paired Fourier eigenvalues give eta=0, and periodic spinors have complex dimension2. Hence the real invariant is (1/2)(2/2)=1/2 modZ. The complex invariant alone would be0 and is not substituted for the real one."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_and_weight_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsToda52"", ""opened_locators"": [""Section4 Theorem(4.1), Corollaries(4.2)–(4.4), and complete printed proof, pp.76–78; text308–446"", ""Original pp.76,77,79 visually opened, including the double-suspension relation at the start of p.79""], ""scope"": ""Theorem4.1 gives [i_n,i_n]=2{h_n}-E(alpha_(n-1)); Corollary4.2 gives E2(alpha_(n-1))=2E{h_n}. Corollary4.3 states that some k-fold suspension pi6(S3)→pi(6+k)(S(3+k)), k>=2, is injective. These groups are in the stable range. Together with the separately opened pi6(S3)=Z/12 and stable pi3=Z/24 tables, the image is the unique order12 subgroup. Thus the order2 stable class12nu determines the unique order2 unstable class6nu-prime. The source convention for the Hopf map is explicitly stated on p.76."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_and_weight_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsBott59"", ""opened_locators"": [""TheoremII and its corollary, pp.314–315; text90–167"", ""Original stable orthogonal period table, printed p.315 (PDF p.4), visually opened""], ""scope"": ""The period for pi_k(O), k=0,...,7, is Z/2,Z/2,0,Z,0,0,0,Z. In positive degree SO has the same homotopy; the universal Spin cover removes pi1 and preserves groups of degree>=2. Hence the stable groups used in B1.1 are pi1Spin=pi2Spin=0, pi3Spin=Z, pi4Spin=0, and pi6SO=0. The six-sphere stable framing difference is zero, and the three-dimensional Spin comparison reduces to H3."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}], ""additional_source_ledgers"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/retained_angle_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/push_C_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/root/classical_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""], ""program_check_records"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_runs/maps_exact.run.json""], ""program_ledgers"": [""deliverables/code/maps_audit/selected_reruns.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/kummer_full_checks.json"", ""deliverables/code/root_maps_F/final_execution_reconciliation.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/audit_notes.md"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json""], ""record"": ""work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json""} Recorded outcome: Passed full receiving proof and exact operative-source checks at the stated scope; historical partial checks and repaired gaps are preserved.. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
