maps:src:B.4.1	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: {""reader"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""full_receiving_proof_read"": true, ""current_check_event_ids"": [""new-maps-homotopy-read-20261117"", ""new-maps-attached-source-scope-20261117:mapsVia2"", ""new-maps-attached-source-scope-20261117:mapsViaLog"", ""new-maps-attached-source-scope-20261117:mapsLR"", ""new-maps-final-small-program-20261117:maps_exact.py""], ""receiving_read_records"": [{""event_id"": ""new-maps-homotopy-read-20261117"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Full arguments read and rederived: stable framing, degree-twelve weighted Hopf factor, retained-angle Arf class, angle-forgotten cone nullhomotopy and conical wedge.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-attached-source-scope-20261117:mapsVia2"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""The actual one-component rank-one normalization, extending chosen section and primitive two independent rank-two periods are printed. The homological matrices in B4.1 are inverse transposes of the source cohomological matrices. The primitive shift evaluates to1/4 on the invariant character; the integral transgression d2(4psi)=1 follows with the same base orientation. Primitive rank-one fundamental-group specialization is also proved directly in the receiving argument by its nodal thimble, independently of the source’s cited Wang propositions.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-attached-source-scope-20261117:mapsViaLog"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""The source acts on columns with its explicit path convention. Its invariant vectors delta,u0,u1 and degrees3k,4l agree under the receiving unimodular comparison PV. Subtracting the pulled-back section conjugates the affine deck action to its linear group action before adding the finite torsion translation. This is the precise source marking used in the generalized quotient statement.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-attached-source-scope-20261117:mapsLR"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""The reduced typeII fibre is a product with two marked circles; the second is the global invariant character. At the cusp the primitive killed lattice is Zh1+Zh3 and xi=h4*. The exact common integral marking gives the displayed order4/order6 monodromies and logarithmic shift e4/4. The Mayer–Vietoris comparison evaluates local minus global extension on the positive meridian to1 and proves d2(4xi)=1 integrally. This is Liu–Rollenske2026, not Lehn–Rollenske–Schinko2019.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-final-small-program-20261117:maps_exact.py"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Full F2^4 invariant-covector enumeration, integral invariant lattices, actual named-family comparison matrices, exact symbolic lens arithmetic, and the flat Pauli symbol. This does not replace the stable-framing or APS geometric argument.""}], ""source_dependency_status"": ""Closed in the exact operative scopes recorded; provider citation/program reviews remain separately itemized rather than inferred from receiving reads."", ""exact_source_check_records"": [{""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/attached_maps_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsVia2"", ""opened_locators"": [""Proposition mum and its complete printed proof, source500–594"", ""Proposition4.2, label mat, complete statement/proof873–941"", ""Proposition5.4, label d2, complete statement/proof1264–1307""], ""scope"": ""The actual one-component rank-one normalization, extending chosen section and primitive two independent rank-two periods are printed. The homological matrices in B4.1 are inverse transposes of the source cohomological matrices. The primitive shift evaluates to1/4 on the invariant character; the integral transgression d2(4psi)=1 follows with the same base orientation. Primitive rank-one fundamental-group specialization is also proved directly in the receiving argument by its nodal thimble, independently of the source’s cited Wang propositions."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/attached_maps_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsViaLog"", ""opened_locators"": [""Lemma2.1 label mono with its complete basis-change proof, source275–346"", ""Actual finite logarithmic data, origin subtraction and action construction, source364–454; prior full logprop/bound proof reading retained in CDP ledger""], ""scope"": ""The source acts on columns with its explicit path convention. Its invariant vectors delta,u0,u1 and degrees3k,4l agree under the receiving unimodular comparison PV. Subtracting the pulled-back section conjugates the affine deck action to its linear group action before adding the finite torsion translation. This is the precise source marking used in the generalized quotient statement."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/attached_maps_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsLR"", ""opened_locators"": [""Lemma3.10 label product at1 and Proposition3.11 label monodromy and specialisation at1, complete proofs893–1014"", ""Propositions3.12–3.13, cusp and global marking, complete proofs1016–1243; Corollary3.16 complete proof1245–1283"", ""Proposition4.8 label Leray differentials, complete statement/proof1568–1671""], ""scope"": ""The reduced typeII fibre is a product with two marked circles; the second is the global invariant character. At the cusp the primitive killed lattice is Zh1+Zh3 and xi=h4*. The exact common integral marking gives the displayed order4/order6 monodromies and logarithmic shift e4/4. The Mayer–Vietoris comparison evaluates local minus global extension on the positive meridian to1 and proves d2(4xi)=1 integrally. This is Liu–Rollenske2026, not Lehn–Rollenske–Schinko2019."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}], ""additional_source_ledgers"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/retained_angle_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/push_C_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/root/classical_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""], ""program_check_records"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_runs/maps_exact.run.json""], ""program_ledgers"": [""deliverables/code/maps_audit/selected_reruns.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/kummer_full_checks.json"", ""deliverables/code/root_maps_F/final_execution_reconciliation.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/audit_notes.md"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json""], ""record"": ""work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json""} Recorded outcome: Passed full receiving proof and exact operative-source checks at the stated scope; historical partial checks and repaired gaps are preserved.. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
