maps:src:B.6.11	2026-11-18T05:21:31.460978+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved as stated Full normalization/trace intersection map, rank-two signature, integral c1 square and spin obstruction on the actual untwisted boundary. The xy=u collar retraction and normalization mapping cylinder give H4(S)→H4(R)→H4(W)→H3(S)=0. Differentiating the principal parameter along each branch gives N_nu=O_R(-D0-Dinfinity). Intersecting the same branch and the two unequal branches yields -a0b0-ainf binf+a0T*binf+b0T*ainf=-U(a)U(b), U=a0-T*ainf. The H4(S) relation maps to zero by the trivial product of conductor normal bundles. From P.O=0, (6P).O=P.(6P)=2 and section square -1, the classes F,m=P-O,v=6P-O-3F have radical F and negative Gram on m,v equal to [[-2,-1],[-1,-6]]. The actual translation is x→x+(x.F)v-(x.v-3x.F)F, checked on F,O,v and fixed component roots; its image plus the relative hyperplane and blow-up divisor spans precisely F,v,m. Thus the filling form is [[2,1],[1,6]], signature2. Tangent-normal and blow-up formulas give nu*c1(W)=pi*F and square zero; H3(S)=0 makes H4(W)→H4(R) injective integrally. H5(W)=0 and the principal central divisor make H2(W)→H2(boundary) an isomorphism. The zero-section curve pairs to1 with c1, so its mod2 restriction is nonzero; the stable complex tangent restriction proves the actual boundary is nonspin. This uses an explicit obstruction, and does not transfer a value to finite logarithmic caps. New derivation after reading the supplied proof; not a blind review and not an independent human check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
