maps:src:B.6.11	2026-11-18T05:22:24.250604+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	used and rechecked in this run	Source mapsShioda90; opened locus: Original journal39(2)(1990): Lemma8.1 and proof p226; Lemmas8.2–8.3 and Theorem8.4 proof pp227–228; Theorem8.6 proof p228; table8.16 and Theorem8.7 proof pp229–230; Theorem8.9 full proof and Corollary8.10 p230; Proposition8.12 full proof and equation8.25 p231. Visually read the original image scan at all listed pages. The unique rational orthogonal-projection divisor gives the equivariant MW map and its torsion kernel; the explicit height formula fixes all section intersections. The narrow lattice proof gives torsion-freeness, integrality, evenness and norm at least2chi; with all fibres irreducible Corollary8.10 identifies the entire MW lattice with that case. Proposition8.12 uses the actual finite base-change pullback of the divisor and scales the pairing by field degree. These are exact classical inputs to the new cyclic-cover/norm and plumbing applications; no generic absence-of-algebraic-classes conclusion is attributed to Shioda. The local-contribution table is numbered8.16, correcting the attached Engel source’s table8.9 citation. Source-opening record only; no additional whole-proof review is inferred.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
