hese are the exact geometric lattice/degree inputs in B6.10–13.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:mapsGriffiths68II"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""A proper holomorphic submersion with compact Kähler fibres over a small polydisc has a holomorphic Hodge-filtration period map in the locally constant marking. The locally simultaneous minimal elliptic pullbacks in B6.12 are smooth projective surfaces and therefore satisfy these hypotheses. Their finite deck characters define holomorphic eigensubbundles. Nonconstant period maps and exclusion of rational Hodge loci then use the separately computed hyperbolic monodromy and signatures.""}], ""source_dependency_status"": ""Closed in the exact operative scopes recorded; provider citation/program reviews remain separately itemized rather than inferred from receiving reads."", ""exact_source_check_records"": [{""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/remaining_primary_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsShioda90"", ""opened_locators"": [""Retained original reprint pagination: standing hypotheses(1.1), p.3; text96–130"", ""Lemma2.7 equation(2.16), Theorem2.8 equations(2.17)–(2.19), p.8; text284–315"", ""Lemmas8.1–8.3, Theorems8.4 and8.6–8.9, Corollary8.10, all complete printed proofs, pp.19–23; text717–928"", ""Proposition8.12 equation(8.25) and complete printed proof, reprint p.24; text935–957""], ""scope"": ""The actual auxiliary surface is smooth projective, relatively minimal, has the pulled-back zero section and singular I1 fibres, so the original standing hypotheses hold. The degree12 extension multiplies height1/6 to2. With chi=1 and no reducible fibres the height formula gives P.O=0 and (P-O)^2=-2. Orthogonal section projection is equivariant and injective modulo torsion; the narrow lattice is even. These are the exact geometric lattice/degree inputs in B6.10–13."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/remaining_primary_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsGriffiths68II"", ""opened_locators"": [""Original journal scan, §II.1(a), precise analytic-fibre-space hypotheses and Theorem(1.1), p.809"", ""Complete printed proof of Theorem(1.1), including Lemmas1.6/1.8/1.10 and Proposition1.11, pp.810–813; text225–518""], ""scope"": ""A proper holomorphic submersion with compact Kähler fibres over a small polydisc has a holomorphic Hodge-filtration period map in the locally constant marking. The locally simultaneous minimal elliptic pullbacks in B6.12 are smooth projective surfaces and therefore satisfy these hypotheses. Their finite deck characters define holomorphic eigensubbundles. Nonconstant period maps and exclusion of rational Hodge loci then use the separately computed hyperbolic monodromy and signatures."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}], ""additional_source_ledgers"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/retained_angle_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/push_C_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/root/classical_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""], ""program_check_records"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_runs/maps_component_periods.run.json""], ""program_ledgers"": [""deliverables/code/maps_audit/selected_reruns.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/kummer_full_checks.json"", ""deliverables/code/root_maps_F/final_execution_reconciliation.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/audit_notes.md"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json""], ""record"": ""work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json""} Recorded outcome: Passed full receiving proof and exact operative-source checks at the stated scope; h