maps:src:B.6.12	2026-11-18T05:21:31.460978+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved as stated outside the specified countable exceptional set Full relative elliptic family, parabolic-cocycle matrices, moving-puncture monodromy, period argument, integral cyclic norm and both automorphism types. Finite direct image identifies each nontrivial H2 character with H1(P1,j_*G): the R0/R2 terms contribute only trivial character, and good reduction/nodal charts give exactly the invariant R1 stalks. The two systems have local image ranks (2,1,1,2) and (2,2,1,2); the rank-two relation and rank-two coboundary maps give dimensions2 and3. The displayed P3/P6 columns satisfy the maps and form quotient bases. Applying the explicit Artin automorphisms and the cocycle rules gives the printed matrices; their commutators have x²-5x+1 and (x-1)(x²-7x+1), checked by the unchanged exact program. A constant positive Hodge line/plane would make these monodromies compact, contradicting those real eigenvalues. Griffiths Theorem1.1 applies to the explicit relative good-reduction smooth projective family. Each one-dimensional nonconstant period map meets a fixed rational (1,1) hyperplane discretely; countably many vectors and marking charts give the stated countable set. Shioda’s unique orthogonal projection is eta-equivariant and embeds MW rationally; irreducible fibres and chi=1 make its integral height even, torsion-free and minimum2. The norm2 section P is primitive; invariant H2 has only three dimensions, so MW^eta=ZP. Absence of Phi2/Phi4 algebraic vectors gives MW^(eta4)=ZP. For (1+eta4+eta8)Q=mP, pairing with P gives3<P,Q>=2m, forcing m=3r; then NQ=12rP, and NP=12P proves equality. Every automorphism covering eta is t_Q eta or t_Q[-1]eta by its actual zero-section image and the nonconstant j-map. Their twelfth powers are the cyclic or alternating norm, respectively; the first misses ±6P and the second is zero because the -1 eigenspace is absent and MW has no torsion. No zero-section argument is applied to torsors. New derivation after reading the supplied proof; not a blind review and not an independent human check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
maps:src:B.6.12	2026-11-18T05:22:24.250604+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	used and rechecked in this run	Source mapsShioda90; opened locus: Original journal39(2)(1990): Lemma8.1 and proof p226; Lemmas8.2–8.3 and Theorem8.4 proof pp227–228; Theorem8.6 proof p228; table8.16 and Theorem8.7 proof pp229–230; Theorem8.9 full proof and Corollary8.10 p230; Proposition8.12 full proof and equation8.25 p231. Visually read the original image scan at all listed pages. The unique rational orthogonal-projection divisor gives the equivariant MW map and its torsion kernel; the explicit height formula fixes all section intersections. The narrow lattice proof gives torsion-freeness, integrality, evenness and norm at least2chi; with all fibres irreducible Corollary8.10 identifies the entire MW lattice with that case. Proposition8.12 uses the actual finite base-change pullback of the divisor and scales the pairing by field degree. These are exact classical inputs to the new cyclic-cover/norm and plumbing applications; no generic absence-of-algebraic-classes conclusion is attributed to Shioda. The local-contribution table is numbered8.16, correcting the attached Engel source’s table8.9 citation. Source-opening record only; no additional whole-proof review is inferred.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
