maps:src:B.6.2	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: {""reader"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""full_receiving_proof_read"": true, ""current_check_event_ids"": [""new-maps-B-remaining-full-20261117:B.6.2"", ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:mapsKrylov03"", ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:mapsRandalWilliams25""], ""receiving_read_records"": [{""event_id"": ""new-maps-B-remaining-full-20261117:B.6.2"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Read the entire synthesis and all retained failed approaches. Checked the endpoint-versus-isotopy distinction for a fractional deck interpolation, the real reflection exponent2 modulo3, and the precise downstream references for the actual zero result.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:mapsKrylov03"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""For M=S3xS3, the framed bounding S3xD4 verifies the hypothesis which makes Theta7 inject into the Torelli group. The quotient is Hom(H3(M),image(pi3SO3→pi3SO4)). The proof of Theorem2 computes the stable Pontryagin number of its generator as absolute value4; therefore the receiving zero integral p1 on the two Wang generators detects the entire normal-framing homomorphism. Theorem3 also gives the quaternionic relation (YUY)^4=Sigma_Milnor^-1 used only as a historical comparison in B6.2.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:mapsRandalWilliams25"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""The theorem concerns the degree-d hypersurface family, d>=3, and obtains the Milnor-sphere subgroup from an actual embedded A2 plumbing and its two Dehn twists. Its proof imports Krylov’s (YUY)^4 relation. B6.2 cites this as an example of the additional smooth identification that would be required by the abandoned plum