maps:src:B.6.4	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: {""reader"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""full_receiving_proof_read"": true, ""current_check_event_ids"": [""new-maps-B-remaining-full-20261117:B.6.4"", ""new-maps-B-program-20261117:maps_mapping_torus_cohom.py"", ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:mapsKrylov03""], ""receiving_read_records"": [{""event_id"": ""new-maps-B-remaining-full-20261117:B.6.4"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Affine return defects; nilpotent fibre connection; the two coinvariant identities; actual local skyscraper classes and their Wang boundary terms; Cech identification of d2; dimension exhaustion and zero swept critical classes; saturated vertical tangent bundle/Koszul sign; integral p1 and Kreck normal-framing implication.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-B-program-20261117:maps_mapping_torus_cohom.py"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Nilpotent differential graded algebra, affine return defects, chain-map identity, cohomology and parabolic quotient dimensions, and critical trace evaluation. This supports the receiving constructible-sheaf argument; it is not independently a global model theorem.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:mapsKrylov03"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""For M=S3xS3, the framed bounding S3xD4 verifies the hypothesis which makes Theta7 inject into the Torelli group. The quotient is Hom(H3(M),image(pi3SO3→pi3SO4)). The proof of Theorem2 computes the stable Pontryagin number of its generator as absolute value4; therefore the receiving zero integral p1 on the two Wang generators detects the entire normal-framing homomorphism. Theorem3 also gives the quaternionic relation (YUY)^4=Sigma_Milnor^-1 used only as a historical comparison in B6.2.""}], ""source_dependency_status"": ""Closed in the exact operative scopes recorded; provider citation/program reviews remain separately itemized rather than inferred from receiving reads."", ""exact_source_check_records"": [{""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/remaining_primary_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""mapsKrylov03"", ""opened_locators"": [""Exact author version arXiv:math/0107005v1,1July2001, not asserted to be a page-identical journal scan"", ""Section2.1, complete definition of the normal-framing homomorphism and equation(2), pp.2–3; text62–122"", ""Theorem2 and complete printed proof, pp.10–12; Theorem3 and its preceding calculation, pp.12–13; text399–555""], ""scope"": ""For M=S3xS3, the framed bounding S3xD4 verifies the hypothesis which makes Theta7 inject into the Torelli group. The quotient is Hom(H3(M),image(pi3SO3→pi3SO4)). The proof of Theorem2 computes the stable Pontryagin number of its generator as absolute value4; therefore the receiving zero integral p1 on the two Wang generators detects the entire normal-framing homomorphism. Theorem3 also gives the quaternionic relation (YUY)^4=Sigma_Milnor^-1 used only as a historical comparison in B6.2."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}], ""additional_source_ledgers"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/retained_angle_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/push_C_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/root/classical_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""], ""program_check_records"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_runs/maps_mapping_torus_cohom.run.json""], ""program_ledgers"": [""deliverables/code/maps_audit/selected_reruns.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_manifest.json"", ""del