lies to any closed spin seven-manifold with torsion spin Pontryagin class; two-connectivity is not a hypothesis of this formula. The displayed invariant is (p_W^2-sigma(W))/8 in Q/28Z with p_W=p1(W)/2. Dividing by28 gives (p1(W)^2-4sigma(W))/896 in Q/Z. The receiving mapping tori are spin and have integral p1=0; both chosen spin structures are tracked by the actual trace."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}], ""additional_source_ledgers"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/retained_angle_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/push_C_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/root/classical_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""], ""program_check_records"": [], ""program_ledgers"": [""deliverables/code/maps_audit/selected_reruns.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/kummer_full_checks.json"", ""deliverables/code/root_maps_F/final_execution_reconciliation.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/audit_notes.md"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json""], ""record"": ""work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json""} Recorded outcome: Passed full receiving proof and exact operative-source checks at the stated scope; historical partial checks and repaired gaps are preserved.. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
maps:src:B.6.5	2026-11-18T05:21:31.460978+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved as stated Complete fixed-s conifold trace, equivariant gluing, integral restrictions, both spin choices and equality of the two smooth sphere classes. The actual substitution x′=x/u identifies the node with the same quadratic equation at fixed s. The germ homotopy r^(-1)F(rz) preserves that equation, extends to its derivative and retains the ruling; its compact reduction acts on D3(Im H)×D4(H) by (v,q)→(gvg^(-1),gqh^(-1)), with (-1,-1) trivial. The boundary faces give the resolution and smoothing using J_v(q)=vq and the tangent vector vq; their shared S2×S3 link and complex orientations agree. The index-three trace W has H3=Z, H4=0, H6=Z; reverse surgery makes its H3 restriction primitive. B6.3 monodromy fixes H3(W), so the Wang map gives an injective H4(Z)→H4(M_s). The current B6.4 p1(M_s)=0 therefore gives integral p1(Z)=0. Relative-to-absolute H4 has zero image, hence signature zero. Simply connected W and its index-three handle extend spin; both parameter-circle lifts remain available. CN2019 §1.4 applies to this closed spin boundary with rationally zero p1 without requiring H4=0. Its divided normalization gives zero trace correction. Cutting the supported six-disc times a parameter interval gives the connected-sum map to the corresponding homotopy sphere, while both product mapping tori bound spin products with zero invariant; this proves a=b. New derivation after reading the supplied proof; not a blind review and not an independent human check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
maps:src:B.6.5	2026-11-18T05:22:24.250604+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	used and rechecked in this run	Source mapsCrowleyNordstrom19; opened locus: Author version3,29December2018: opening spin conventions p1; Section1.4 equations(2)–(3), p5; Remark2.36 p24. Read the exact formula and its index/gluing justification: for a closed spin seven-manifold whose spin characteristic class p_M is torsion, (p_W²−sigma(W))/8 is independent of spin coboundary in Q/28Z. The source states no H4 torsion-free hypothesis here. With p_W=p1(W)/2 and division by28 this is (p1²−4sigma)/896 in Q/Z. B6.5 uses its integral-p1-zero trace; B6.15 uses the same formula for torsion p1 on an H4=Z⊕Z/|k| boundary. This matches the received mapsCrowleyNordstrom19 author/title/arXiv/DOI10.1112/plms.12222. CrowleyNordstrom2019 is declared only as an identical-work source-key alias, with the same authors/title/DOI; no separate pre-existing bibliography entry of that name was found and no separate reading is counted. Source-opening record only; no additional whole-proof review is inferred.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
