maps:src:B.6.6	2026-11-18T05:21:31.460978+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved as stated for the stipulated fixed-data, reference-cusp families Full all-coprime analytic smoothing, actual fixed-data return, Leray representatives and conifold comparison; no numerical equality between different families inferred. For h=2kl the finite quotient charts retain their free actions, and the factor 1-st is a holomorphic unit. Fixed-data comparison vectors have first coordinate zero, so replacing beta by beta-L_s leaves their affine and power vectors unchanged. The cusp defect lies in Zw+Zd; its two integral powers extend to the separated node charts and preserve the actual smoothing parameter. The vertical Lie sequence 0→O→V→O(-p0)→0 has H1=0 over the displayed two-chart Stein base, giving the holomorphic Cech correction covering the identity on s and B and respecting the chosen resolution. Scaling the central shear from 2 to h scales the exact parabolic coboundaries by h/2. On the regular nilpotent piece dtheta=h kappa gamma and first-coordinate-zero transitions preserve gamma; the new node has dtheta=(alpha+h kappa)gamma and the two displayed Wang representatives are -[gamma upsilon]/h and -[gamma omega]/h. They exhaust the primitive H3 image and restrict trivially to the swept critical curves. The saturated tangent sequence therefore gives integral p1=0 and the same B6.5 trace identifies the central smoothing class with this family’s own original class. The unchanged parabolic-cohomology program was read and replayed, separately from this geometric descent. New derivation after reading the supplied proof; not a blind review and not an independent human check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
