maps:src:B.6.7	2026-11-18T05:21:31.460978+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved counterexample; the rejected ordinary scalar-shear assertion remains refuted Full ordinary-bundle fundamental-group obstruction, integral gauge quotient and exact order-six class. The ordinary bundle group is Lambda semidirect F(a1,a2). A homotopy over the base changes its two affine defects by one simultaneous integral coboundary. Quotienting Lambda by the invariant delta direction permits all circle-gauge corrections. The resulting six-row system has unique rational solution (1/6,0,0) and Smith factors (1,1,6), so no integral solution exists and the obstruction has exact order six. Changing marking adds the same coboundary; changing base lifts contributes (S-I)r in Z delta, already killed. Since S fixes both defect vectors, the r-fold return has r times the obstruction. The full sixfold residual defects are -4delta and 3delta; a literal global gamma-coordinate interpolation would require nonintegral base windings 1/3 and -1/4. These are exact semidirect-product morphisms and do not evaluate a smooth sphere invariant. New derivation after reading the supplied proof; not a blind review and not an independent human check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
