maps:src:B.6.8	2026-11-18T05:21:31.460978+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved as stated Complete symbolic fixed-twist quotient obstruction for all coprime pairs, with no multiplicity cutoff. Writing b=4lN0+3kN1=±1 and h=2kl, the actual defects are ell1=(0,0,-2lN0,0), ell2=(0,-kN1,0,0). Their finite norms equal -hN0 delta and -hN1 delta, while -M0(ell1+A1ell2)=(0,0,2lN0-kN1,kN1) lies in the permitted cusp plane. The unique quotient coboundary is ((4lN0-3kN1)/6,2lN0-kN1,2kN1-2lN0); its first coordinate is b/6-kN1 and thus has exact denominator six. In the original case its difference from B6.7 is the integral coboundary (-1,-3,4). The symbolic program checks the actual maps for arbitrary symbols, with no finite search and no implication about the family’s Theta7 residue. New derivation after reading the supplied proof; not a blind review and not an independent human check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
