maps:src:E.1.5	2026-11-18	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved Read and re-derived the complete integral proof. The actual unimodular finite-root change of basis identifies each reduced fibre with a five-torus mapping torus. Cutting its root circle proves the norm-map formula on Wang kernels without choosing a splitting. The two covering cokernels, complete global horizontal three-form maps, and all local torsion kernels were recomputed exactly; the combined norm/image matrix has eight unit Smith factors. The original bielliptic section has even intersection form, so the global two-form maps onto the order-two cokernel. The full parabolic coboundary torsion restricts with orders3,2,1 and leaves no parabolic torsion. Naturality from X and the degree-one elliptic section divisor kill the two primitive target summands integrally. The free Leray extensions, UCT and Poincare duality give every asserted torsion-free homology group. Source proofs and historical checks were available; this is a re-derivation, not a blind check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
