maps:src:E.2.1	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Recomputed the root-stack degree formula for k=0,1,-1,-2 and the split direct images from the actual cusp cup product and invariant covector. K_X=L^-6 and Weierstrass adjunction plus the actual small crepant resolution give K_Z=Pi*L^-5. Fibres of Pi remain dimension one even over the toric deeper strata; flatness and relative duality give R1Pi*O=L^-1. The section splits the derived unit, so the two acyclic root twists yield h0q=(1,1,0,0,0). A meromorphic trivialization of L makes x generically degree two to X×P1, proving a=2 via symmetric functions. Read the original Jia–Meng Theorem1.1/Remark1.2 p2, Esole–Kang equations1.2–1.4 pp3–4, and Peters–Sterk Theorem2.2.1 with full proof p61. Checked c1=0, c4=6, c2²=2, signature2 and the positive rank-two unimodular lattice I2. Only universal characteristic polynomials are imported from the algebraic Weierstrass source."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [""Original JiaMeng2022 arXiv2201.06748v1 p2"", ""Original EsoleKang2018 arXiv1807.08755v1 pp3–4"", ""PetersSterk June2024 author draft p61, Theorem2.2.1 and full proof""], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""E1.4 and E1.3 dependencies as separately scoped"", ""Original root-stack analytic duality/base-change already opened in CDP records""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [{""key"": ""ffJiaMeng"", ""locator"": ""arXiv2201.06748v1,18January2022, p2, Theorem1.1 and Remark1.2; preceding paragraph credit to Demailly–Paun"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}, {""key"": ""ffEsoleKang"", ""locator"": ""arXiv1807.08755v1,23July2018, pp3–4, equations(1.2)–(1.4)"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}, {""key"": ""ffPetersSterk"", ""locator"": ""Author June2024 draft, printed p61(PDF p68), Theorem2.2.1 and its complete proof"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}], ""shared_dependency_records"": [{""source_id"": ""Paper II root-stack direct-image/duality input"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/references_verified.json"", ""scope"": ""Proper flat curve duality, base change and actual root-chart descent were opened in the completed PaperII audit.""}, {""source_id"": ""MAPS E1.3/E1.4"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/result_audit.json"", ""scope"": ""The geometric cusp specialization and newly independent six-dimensional exterior page supply the required topology.""}], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/retur