maps:src:E.2.10	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read and rederived the complete marked knot-group and both spinning obstructions. Removing the regular base disc leaves a^3=h,b^4=h^-1 and the unfilled meridian ab. The free-product quotient proves peripheral Z² injectivity. Its unique zero-linking framing has theta=-12gamma, so g maps to h*mu^-12 and u,w,d die. Boundary restrictions give -12gamma*u and -12gamma*w, forcing their common contraction radical into Z*d, while a degree-three class ±2gamma*u*w is killed by d. For an ordinary triple spin, the original longitude lies in the degree-two radical but remains nontrivial; for a single spin of arbitrary T3, the exact cap MV gives R²=R_L² and R³=R_L² wedge s, so contraction by the spin circle must be injective on R³. Both contradictions use the full embedded peripheral/zero-linking data, not merely the abstract knot group."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [""E2.6 full marked boundary maps; B5.2 exact original cap presentation as separately assigned""], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""Winter2008 original ordinary-spin definition and Theorem4.5 opening"", ""maps_shifted_pi2.py contraction certificate rerun""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [{""key"": ""mapsWinter08"", ""locator"": ""arXiv:0711.1638v3 (7 August 2008), Section 3 p.4, ordinary-spin paragraph before Theorem 3.4 and its proof; Sections 4–4.1 pp.7–10, peripheral definitions, Theorem 4.5 and full proof, following longitude qualification."", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}], ""shared_dependency_records"": [{""source_id"": ""MAPS B5.2"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_full_checks.json"", ""scope"": ""Complete cap/peripheral receiving proof, event new-maps-B-remaining-full-20261117:B.5.2. Its separate full B-program reruns remain with maps_audit; the E-specific certificate has already passed.""}], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
maps:src:E.2.10	2026-11-18	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved Read and re-derived the full marked knot-group and both ordinary-spinning obstructions. Van Kampen retains the unfilled meridian ab, and its infinite-order image in C3*C4 proves peripheral Z2 injection. The unique zero-linking section has theta=-12gamma and sends g to h*(ab)^-12. Actual boundary restrictions contain -12gamma*u and -12gamma*w, whose simultaneous radical is the d line; the class plus/minus2gamma*u*w is killed by that line. The explicit spun-complement decomposition gives the incompatible restriction and contraction properties for triple spin and every single spin of a T3. Winter’s ordinary-spin definition p4 and Theorem4.5 pp9–10 were opened with the longitude-up-to-inverse qualification. All sixteen marked boundary certificates passed. Source proofs and historical checks were available; this is a re-derivation, not a blind check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
