maps:src:E.2.11	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read and checked the entire homological, cohomological and module argument. The three retained degree-two boundary coordinates theta*g1,theta*g2,g1*g2 vanish on kerD2 in that order; naturality gives c_*H3=0. In target MV, the two primitive relations leave v=gamma1*gamma2 as the free H3 connecting generator; source images contain12v and every v coefficient is divisible by12, so c^* has exact order12. The relative universal-cover pair is2-connected and its degree-three Hurewicz group is pi2(P), so H3(N,P)=(pi2P)_G and H2(N,P)=0. UCT identifies evaluation on the injected z with12Z, forcing gcd(12,e1,...,e7)=1 in the complete extension presentation. Its Smith factors give Z²+Z12^6. A projective group-ring module would have free abelian coinvariants, and the specified connected sums add only free induced pi2 modules."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""maps_shifted_pi2.py full integral boundary certificates rerun"", ""E2.6 and E2.9 dependencies as separately scoped""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [], ""shared_dependency_records"": [], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
maps:src:E.2.11	2026-11-18	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved Read and re-derived the complete relative homotopy/extension calculation. The literal quotient retains only gamma1,gamma2,theta; the three corresponding degree-two boundary coordinates vanish on the integral MV kernel, proving c_*H3=0. The target connecting generator pulls back to a class of exact order12: 12v is in the actual source image and every v coefficient is divisible by12. Relative Hurewicz on universal covers identifies H3(N,P) with the desired coinvariant module. Evaluation on its injected Z has image12Z, fixing the primitive seven-component extension vector. Its exact Smith form gives Z2 plus(Z/12)^6. The projective-module and sphere-product obstructions follow by the actual split coinvariant maps, not a rank comparison. All sixteen coordinate/sign certificates passed. Source proofs and historical checks were available; this is a re-derivation, not a blind check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
