maps:src:E.2.12	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read all239 lines and rederived the actual group-ring localization proof. Explicit unimodular row/column operations reduce B(z) to diag(1,z-1,z-1) with one zero column; its transpose is injective. The infinite-cylinder normalization has no degree-two extension or possible higher differential, giving H2=A+(A/(z-1))² and H4=A. Injected central Z² makes R free over its Laurent subring, so localization is flat and both central differences are non-zero-divisors. Regular torus Koszul complexes contract after h1-1 inversion; finite caps have pure-translation mth powers and die. The sole surviving first cusp induces the two shifted T3 exterior algebras over R1/(h2-1), giving ranks1,3,4,4,3,1. Before localization the regular/boundary two-stage filtrations are killed by I², caps by q=(h1-1)(h2-1), and MV gives q²H*=0 without a splitting assumption. Infinite rank follows from the surviving central Laurent submodule, ruling out a finite-type universal cover and a compact-fibre pi1-isomorphic fibration overN."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""manifolds_cusp_alexander.py exact Laurent matrix rerun"", ""E2.9 central subgroup injection as separately scoped""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [], ""shared_dependency_records"": [], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
maps:src:E.2.12	2026-11-18	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved Read and re-derived the complete group-ring localization proof. The actual gamma-cyclic cusp normalization has the displayed unimodular Laurent reduction and ordinary compactly supported chains, yielding A plus two A/(h-1) degree-two summands. The full central Z2 injection makes the localizations flat. Literal regular-torus Koszul contractions and the finite affine power actions kill every other piece; the surviving cusp induces the stated R1/(h2-1) modules with multiplicities1,3,4,4,3,1. Before localization the two-stage graph and Wang filtrations are killed by I squared, so the two-term MV extension gives q squared as a uniform annihilator. The nonzero central Laurent submodule proves infinite rational rank and the stated compact-fibre obstruction. The exact Laurent certificate passed. Source proofs and historical checks were available; this is a re-derivation, not a blind check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
