maps:src:E.2.13	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read and rederived the complete actual circle fibration and return argument. Averaging the integral primitive class over the torus action gives alpha(V1)=12 and alpha(V2)=-12. At every point an unchanged regular factor maps its g-vector to one of these fields, so the pulled-back form is nowhere zero on the actual map. Primitivity gives connected fibre. The mod12 cone-character kernel is torsion free with Euler-10 and genus6; its central kernel is generated by h1*h2. Independently checked the weighted Hopf connection and orientation integral1/12, yielding the two pulled-back Euler entries(-1,-1) and diagonal-circle Euler-1. Localizations force faithful action of the whole central Z² on pi2. Every finite-index subgroup has centralizer contained in this centre; an S1 product factor would contradict faithfulness. A stable letter of character1 acts inner on kerchi exactly when its exponent is divisible by12, while no positive return power is homotopic to identity."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""Scott83 exact orbifold classification and Euler covering formula opening"", ""maps_shifted_circle.py integral character/Euler rerun"", ""A2.1 literal quotient-map derivative checked by maps_audit""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [{""key"": ""rootScott83"", ""locator"": ""Bull. London Math. Soc. 15 (1983), pp.424–428, Theorems 2.3–2.5 and orbifold Euler-characteristic discussion; pp.434–436, circle Euler convention, Lemma 3.5 and Theorem 3.6."", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}], ""shared_dependency_records"": [{""source_id"": ""MAPS A2.1"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/paperI_circle_quotient_manifest.json"", ""scope"": ""Actual circle quotient and derivative, printed in PaperI.""}], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
