maps:src:E.2.14	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read all307 lines and checked the actual splice, return and rational variation. The two maps xi_E-12gamma2 and12gamma1-xi_E agree on the full product collar; their regular-circle derivatives stay nonzero. Their level is the connected E12 cover timesT3, with theta1prime=gamma2-gamma1 and opposite second marking. The interpolated vector field has d(rho)=1; its time12 map is exactly the primitive diagonal torus twist, identity at both collar ends. The deRham/prism variation is boundary-connecting composed with contraction and restriction, so its square vanishes. Noninvariant deck eigenspaces restrict to zero, making the displayed invariant boundary matrices sufficient for the variation. Recomputed the ring-product sign normalization c2=-2,c3=2. The actual affine character transports are lambda^4 A1^-t,lambda^-3 A2^-t,M0^-t, and the punctured-disc graph has no H2. Summing the six character-order rows with multiplicities1,1,2,2,2,4 gives E12 ranks(1,7,46,56,46,6,0). MV then gives the stated fibre Betti vector; Wang fixes precisely one size-two eigenvalue-one Jordan block in degrees4/5, all other blocks semisimple."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""maps_shifted_return.py and maps_shifted_cover.py full exact matrix reruns"", ""Original sphere integral cusp specialization is in the separately checked B5.16 context""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [], ""shared_dependency_records"": [{""source_id"": ""Equations B.5.16–B.5.18"", ""record"": ""sources/returns/S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS/sections/maps_B.tex"", ""scope"": ""This reader additionally read/rederived lines1030–1171: degree-two honeycomb quotient, primitive swept-torus kernel, both actual boundary coefficients and retained regular framed tube. These are equation tags, not unproved result IDs.""}, {""source_id"": ""MAPS B5.1"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_and_weight_source_checks.json"", ""scope"": ""Waldhausen Theorem6.1 p77 matched to the relative marked topological cusp comparison; full receiving proof and all boundary hypotheses retained in maps_B_and_weight_application_checks.json.""}], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
