maps:src:E.2.15	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read the entire integral proof and checked all extension arguments. The regular permutation coefficient lattice avoids integral averaging: finite lifted caps are genuine torus root covers and cusp sheets unchanged, so each stalk is the primitive invariant lattice. Hermite bases of im(T_i-I) preserve indices in the graph map; its Smith primitivity must be checked by the retained program. Free E12 groups imply free piece relative groups by Poincare–Lefschetz, so the actual boundary image is the saturation of its known rational span. The common-boundary lattice is obtained from ker[A,-B] because each A/B is an injective column basis. Integral prism variation applies also to possible torsion output; rank-one Smith72 in degrees4/5 lies in a primitive free MV summand. A primitive factorization72*u*ell with ell(u)=0 yields the stated shear normal form. Wang gives all covers; only degrees3/7 have a potentially absorbing torsion extension, and the10-dimensional integral linking pairing fixes them from the already settled degrees8/4. UCT gives exactly the homological torsion list and the distinguishing order72n."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""maps_shifted_cover_integral.py and maps_shifted_fibre_integral.py complete Hermite/Smith transforms rerun"", ""E2.14 actual collar and E12 boundary marking""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [], ""shared_dependency_records"": [], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
