maps:src:E.2.16	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read all429 lines and rederived the derived cusp comparison and full integral presentation. The boundary mapping cone has H1=A/(q²)+A/(q); the actual normalized component intersections give 2-h-h^-1, hence a unit Ext1 component modulo q². Since all displayed homology modules have projective dimension at most one, the derived splitting and triangular target changes remove exactly the stated extension components while preserving the full external map. Every unit modulo q² lifts to ±h^n. The terminal-strip exterior chain lift and the finite winding norm use the actual maps, with the negative fourth-root norm and phase-degree norms kept distinct. Checked injectivity of the Fox column via (a-1)N_a=q, the pure augmentation reductions, and both redundant final relations. The induced cyclic-sign extension has nonzero class in Z/2, preserves the injection of the invariant infinite-order t, and gives the equivalent cyclic presentation after replacing x by x+t. The peripheral homology and all ten degree-two chain columns are retained separately; the nonzero free coefficient on gTheta is not discarded."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [""Full source maps_complement_module.tex, including the actual terminal-strip comparison and final peripheral prism identity""], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""maps_complement_module.py exact noncommutative chain/cancellation/peripheral certificate source reading and rerun"", ""E2.12 exact Laurent calculation and original cusp specialization equationsB.5.16–17""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [], ""shared_dependency_records"": [{""source_id"": ""Equations B.5.16–B.5.17"", ""record"": ""sources/returns/S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS/sections/maps_B.tex"", ""scope"": ""Exact normalization/cusp peripheral maps re-read at lines1030–1171; the independently verified E2.12 Laurent calculation and E2.16 full noncommutative certificate retain all maps.""}], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
