maps:src:E.2.17	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read all380 lines and rederived the kernel-complex construction and every abstract module reduction. The complement projection to its one-relator aspherical spine keeps the actual Fox peripheral column; its degree-two Fox column is injective, so projection extends over the full higher complex. The aspherical splice target retains its degree-four cell, avoiding a false truncated acyclicity argument. The degreewise split kernel has six unit degree-one pairs; after cancellation its H2 is the explicit34-by123 presentation. Both normal-circle inversion and product-order signs were checked. Pure norm relations kill the previously unassigned central differences before passing to the orbifold group ring. The seven-generator change has determinant1; substituting its inverse gives t1=OmegaL and eliminates that generator with a unit coefficient. The two cyclic axes have no common central kernel. Coinvariants give six Z12 factors. Restricting to the actual circle-fibre group has index12 on each axis because chi(hi)=±12 and injects there; hence24 free group-ring generators. The remaining surface-group restriction and its144-by240 exact Smith calculation are separate from any smooth-type assertion."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""maps_splice_module.py exact amalgam normal form, full presentation reductions and coinvaria