maps:src:E.2.3	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read and rederived the entire group and rational Leray calculation. Each cusp kills its two angular generators and its meridian, and normal closure under A1 kills u; the finite gluing leaves central gamma,gamma-prime with the exact two3rd/fourth-power relations and product relation. The hyperbolic S2(3,4,3,4) orbifold has Euler-5/6; its principal torus orbibundle gives injection of the central Z². Recomputed the abelian relation matrix. The exterior direct-image Euler polynomial uses four finite and two cusp points; its H1 row and tensor transgression supports are correct. Even invariant-to-coinvariant pairings are nonzero and odd ones zero, so the displayed d2 ranks determine all Betti numbers without a degeneration assumption. Admissible Mobius transformations form a path-connected complex-hypersurface complement and proper smooth transport preserves orientation."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [""Original sphere transgressions are supplied by the complete PaperI topology proof""], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""Original Scott hyperbolic-orbifold theorem opening"", ""Exact rational matrix program rerun""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": 