maps:src:E.2.8	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read the complete disc-extension construction. B2.1 null-homotopy gives a smooth D7 extension fixed on a boundary collar. Relative transversality is required only at the second map’s three critical values. At all other values df2 is onto; at those three, dF is onto. The resulting eleven-dimensional inverse image has boundary exactly P and its inverse-image orientation agrees with the complex boundary orientation. The pulled-back normal2-plane comes from the contractible D7. Any two boundary choices agree up to homotopy because [S6,SO2]=H1(S6,Z)=0. The bounding second-sphere framing and outward collar normal give exactly the specified natural boundary stable framing."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""Original Hirsch Chapter3 section2 Theorems2.1/2.5 and relative-cutoff hypotheses opening"", ""B2.1 exact null-homotopy is assigned to maps_audit; retain its current gate""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [{""key"": ""rootHirsch76"", ""locator"": ""Grad