maps:src:E.2.9	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: [{""id"": ""full-receiving-proof-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified."", ""details"": ""Read and rederived the full aspherical target and framed bordism proof. Weighted Hopf critical pairs are disjoint, so their fibre product is a smooth closed four-manifold. Primitive finite translations make the torus orbibundle total space smooth; the good hyperbolic orbifold cover is H² and its torus-bundle pullback is trivial, yielding universal cover H²×R². The literal quotient maps carry the exact six generators identically, so c induces the stated pi1 isomorphism. Abelian character(4,-3,-4,3,12,-12), duality and Euler0 give homology(S1×S3). The stable splitting(S3)+=S0∨S3 separates each bounding sphere’s zero component and the specific eta³ map component. All four external-product components vanish, the last by eta4=0. Transverse inverse image of N in a framed13-bordism has the required11-dimensional filling overBG, and the normal framing pulled from the first S3 agrees with E2.8 after pullback. This is a bordism statement only; no smooth classification is inferred."", ""extra_source_scopes"": [], ""outcome"": ""complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope"", ""remaining_dependencies"": [""Original Scott83 and Davis–Kirk01 theorem openings"", ""Use the already opened IWX2023 Table1 p113 for pi4S=0, explicitly recording the different edition"", ""B1.2 eta³ class and A2.1/B2.1 actual maps are assigned to maps_audit"", ""shifted_group_bordism.py arithmetic rerun""]}, {""id"": ""maps-E-source-program-closure-20261117"", ""reader"": {""model"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""timezone"": ""UTC"", ""reader"": ""/root/cdp_audit""}, ""scope"": ""Exact operative primary sources, shared receiving-proof dependencies, all assigned original programs and the independent E1.4 exterior page."", ""references"": [{""key"": ""rootScott83"", ""locator"": ""Bull. London Math. Soc. 15 (1983), pp.424–428, Theorems 2.3–2.5 and orbifold Euler-characteristic discussion; pp.434–436, circle Euler convention, Lemma 3.5 and Theorem 3.6."", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}, {""key"": ""rootDavisKirk01"", ""locator"": ""Graduate Studies in Mathematics 35 (2001), pp.206–210: Theorem 8.13, Corollary 8.15, Definition 8.16, Theorem 8.17 and the complete supplied proof outline; stable-stem table p.208."", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}, {""key"": ""IsaksenWangXu2023"", ""locator"": ""Publications mathématiques de l’IHÉS 137 (2023), pp.112–113, Corollary 1.3, the table convention, and Table 1 rows 3, 4 and 6."", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}, {""key"": ""rootHirsch76"", ""locator"": ""Graduate Texts in Mathematics 33 (1976), Chapter 3, Section 2: pp.74–78, Theorems 2.1, 2.2, 2.5, Lemma 2.3, and their supplied proofs."", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""}], ""shared_dependency_records"": [{""source_id"": ""MAPS A2.1"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/paperI_circle_quotient_manifest.json"", ""scope"": ""Literal circle quotient with the actual map is printed in PaperI as mapsI:src:A.2.1.""}, {""source_id"": ""MAPS B1.1/B1.2"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_and_weight_application_checks.json"", ""scope"": ""Full receiving proofs and Bott/APS/Toda originals are closed. In addition, this reader read maps_B.tex lines1–150 and independently followed the invariant stable-framing restriction and the product Lie-torus calculation. The E2.9 vanishing only needs st[e]=eta^3 and pi4S=0, not the separate real-e or unstable normalization.""}], ""outcome"": ""No unaddressed mathematical objection remains in this assigned receiving proof; all E-specific source and program checks are completed."", ""scope_limit"": ""This does not certify unrelated portions of the external literature or replace separately owned B/D full-program records.""}] Recorded outcome: complete receiving proof independently checked; operative source matches and E-specific exact programs completed. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
