maps:src:F.3.10	2026-11-17	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_09_PAPERS	targeted proof check	"Received S6_09 writing record: {""reader"": ""GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode)"", ""effort"": ""Pro"", ""date"": ""2026-11-17"", ""full_receiving_proof_read"": true, ""current_check_event_ids"": [""new-fourfold-read-20261117"", ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:ffAlarconForstneric25"", ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:ffForstnericPrezelj02""], ""receiving_read_records"": [{""event_id"": ""new-fourfold-read-20261117"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""Full proofs of listed statements read except the still unresolved geometric d2 identification in F.2.6. Exact matrix, discriminant, period and LSAP-tube programs pass. The actual LSAP bundle-section theorem, Nagy inertia theorem and Jin statements have been opened.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:ffAlarconForstneric25"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""The printed spanning tubes supply LSAP, and Proposition7.13(d), rather than the unresolved general Oka-1 fibre-bundle question7.10, supplies the section theorem. For F3.10 the vertical spray dominates on the attaching discs away from the finite fixed-jet set, exactly as in5.6–5.8. At a critical arc the compact set has the Mergelyan property; the fixed jet points lie in its interior. After a holomorphic frame is chosen, Theorem2.13 applies to Grassmannian-valued maps, leaving the base coordinate fixed.""}, {""event_id"": ""new-maps-primary-scope-20261117:ffForstnericPrezelj02"", ""record"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json"", ""scope"": ""The frame bundle over the open Riemann surface is a holomorphic submersion over a Stein base with fibre GL(n,C). Its global vertical spray is (g,A)→g exp(A), and its derivative is onto the vertical tangent. A complex bundle over a graph has a continuous frame because GL(n,C) is connected. Theorem1.2 deforms that section to a holomorphic frame, which is the only use in F3.10.""}], ""source_dependency_status"": ""Closed in the exact operative scopes recorded; provider citation/program reviews remain separately itemized rather than inferred from receiving reads."", ""exact_source_check_records"": [{""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/remaining_primary_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""ffAlarconForstneric25"", ""opened_locators"": [""Published2025 full text: Definitions2.1,7.7,7.11, Theorem2.2, Proposition7.13 and its printed proof"", ""Lemma5.1 spray construction and gluing, equations5.6–5.8; Theorem2.13 exact Mergelyan/jet statement; extracted text1390–1451,1096–1102,1664–1775""], ""scope"": ""The printed spanning tubes supply LSAP, and Proposition7.13(d), rather than the unresolved general Oka-1 fibre-bundle question7.10, supplies the section theorem. For F3.10 the vertical spray dominates on the attaching discs away from the finite fixed-jet set, exactly as in5.6–5.8. At a critical arc the compact set has the Mergelyan property; the fixed jet points lie in its interior. After a holomorphic frame is chosen, Theorem2.13 applies to Grassmannian-valued maps, leaving the base coordinate fixed."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/remaining_primary_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""ffForstnericPrezelj02"", ""opened_locators"": [""Exact author version3,7May2002; Definition1.1, Theorem1.2 and Example1, printed p.3; text90–132""], ""scope"": ""The frame bundle over the open Riemann surface is a holomorphic submersion over a Stein base with fibre GL(n,C). Its global vertical spray is (g,A)→g exp(A), and its derivative is onto the vertical tangent. A complex bundle over a graph has a continuous frame because GL(n,C) is connected. Theorem1.2 deforms that section to a holomorphic frame, which is the only use in F3.10."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}], ""additional_source_ledgers"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/retained_angle_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/push_C_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/root/classical_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""], ""program_check_records"": [], ""program_ledgers"": [""deliverables/code/maps_audit/selected_reruns.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/kummer_full_checks.json"", ""deliverables/code/root_maps_F/final_execution_reconciliation.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/audit_notes.md"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json""], ""record"": ""work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json""} Recorded outcome: Passed full receiving proof and exact operative-source checks at the stated scope; historical partial checks and repaired gaps are preserved.. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
