maps:src:F.3.3	2026-11-18T02:43:58.020152+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved Explicit synthesis deductions, Oka section lifting and primitive lattice comparison Read and re-derived the two synthesis propositions and supplied their previously absent numbered deduction proofs in the final text. For the open-base period theorem, the flat transition action is holomorphic, the fibre has the proved LSAP, and the opened v5 Definition7.7/Proposition7.13(d) applies to sections; the connected fibre supplies a section over the graph retract. Real transversality makes the holomorphic quotient a proper torus family with the stated lattice. Rechecked P1.2: the primitive-to-quotient wedge map has Smith (1,1,1,1,2); unimodularity identifies the quotient with the primitive dual, and the one-dimensional invariant-form spaces with primitive determinants -2 and -16 exclude every alternative integral intertwiner.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
