only at rank=length, whereas 3>1 here. The unique-genus conclusion applies. The extension to the odd unimodular ambient lattice is proved directly by its unique order-two gluing graph; the source theorem is applied only to the even complement."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/fourfold_priority_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""ffBHS"", ""opened_locators"": [""Version2, December2,2019; conventions §1.2 p.6"", ""Recollections2.2–2.3 p.7; Definitions2.4–2.5 and Theorem2.6 p.8; p.8 visually verified""], ""scope"": ""The Wall theorem is stated for closed smooth oriented (n-1)-connected 2n-manifolds; all diffeomorphisms preserve orientation. For n=4 the middle lattice and normal-bundle function determine the connected-sum orbit under Theta8. The receiving proof reconstructs the rank-four normal clutching class from its Euler and Pontryagin numbers: (a,b) maps to (a-b,-2(a+b)), an injective homomorphism. Thus matching intersection forms and p1 matches the full n-space, not merely its stable rational image."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/fourfold_priority_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""ffNagy2026"", ""opened_locators"": [""Publisher Theorem1.4; §1.4 Theorems1.7–1.8"", ""§9 Definition9.1, Propositions9.2/9.5/9.6/9.7, Theorem9.8 and final proofs of1.8/1.4; complete mathematical text opened, including the divisibility conversion"", ""Searchable original extraction nagy_paragraphs.txt31–32,49–59,564–600; complete §9 extraction nagy_section9_complete.txt1–504""], ""scope"": ""The exact theorem gives I(M)=0 iff p1 is divisible by8 for a closed 3-connected 8-manifold; otherwise I(M)=Theta8=Z/2. Its §9 proof identifies the normal-type bordism kernel and uses q=4 in the free-Hq Q-form theorem. The final formula d_M=2 alpha_M makes the criterion 4|alpha_M equivalent to8|d_M. The receiving manifold has p1=2(1,1,1,1), divisibility2; therefore both homotopy-sphere possibilities are absorbed with the given orientation."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}, {""ledger"": ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/fourfold_priority_source_checks.json"", ""key"": ""ffMandal"", ""opened_locators"": [""Attached original source lines1–315: title, conventions, Theorems1.1/1.3, Corollary1.4"", ""Lines465–564: connected-sum cohomology and normalized Pontryagin formula with printed proof"", ""Section5 lines1398–1493: Corollary1.4 complete proof and precise orientation qualification""], ""scope"": ""The original criterion concerns the stated orientation on l HP2 # m(-HP2): almost-complex existence iff l=2m+1 with m odd. The proof substitutes p1=2 sum x_i, p2=7(l-m)u and Euler number l+m+2 in the stable congruence and Euler obstruction. At (l,m)=(3,1) both conditions hold. The normalized basis and sign on the negatively oriented summand agree with F1.3 and the comparison manifold of F4.1."", ""status"": ""verified in the specified scope""}], ""additional_source_ledgers"": [""deliverables/work/maps_audit/references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/retained_angle_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/invariants_arithmetic/push_C_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/root/classical_references_verified.json"", ""deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_E/references_verified.json""], ""program_check_records"": [], ""program_ledgers"": [""deliverables/code/maps_audit/selected_reruns.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/maps_B_remaining_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/final_small_program_manifest.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/kummer_full_checks.json"", ""deliverables/code/root_maps_F/final_execution_reconciliation.json"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/audit_notes.md"", ""deliverables/work/maps_audit/check_events.json""], ""record"": ""work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json""} Recorded outcome: Passed full receiving proof and exact operative-source checks at the stated scope; historical partial checks and repaired gaps are preserved.. This continuation preserves the earlier scope; pre-reading derivation order is not inferred."		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
