night:P3F.35	2026-11-18T05:22:16.352601+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved Complete one-vertex fan classification, actual periodic flops and prime fixed-set budget Read and rederived the complete proof. Area one and unimodularity force two triangle and three edge orbits. From triangle(0,a,b), the three actual edge classes force every adjacent triangle and the basis fan T(a,b−a). Replacing its diagonal implements exactly T(v−w,w); reversing the other selected diagonal implements T(v+w,w). Euclid on the primitive first-coordinate row terminates by these individual integral column moves. In each edge orbit the actual curves are disjoint, have no lattice stabilizer and have the conifold relation r0+r2=r1+r3. The common blowup has normal O(−1,−1) on P1xP1, giving the two actual ruling contractions. Its integral cohomology splitting is primitive by exceptional degree−1, and general position plus van Kampen preserve pi1. The already opened Smale/KM63 inputs give the smooth six-sphere from these exact groups. For primitive delta=av+bw, the quotient-lattice maps give isotropy orders |b|,|a|,|a−b|. A prime divides at most one; the determinant-one triangle weights have sum zero and gcd one, so each fixed chart is its origin or one axis. The actual gluings give one complete P1 or exactly two points, each of total mod-prime Betti number two. Regular-fibre primitivity excludes escaping components. A separate nonfree cap contributes an additional compact fixed component and violates the currently opened Floyd Thm4.4 bound. This proves cap freeness for all allowed fans, without asserting global semifreeness for every such fan. Original AC Proposition9.24/Remarks9.25–26 pp82–83 supply the known reference-fan special case and are now expressly credited; no novelty claim is inferred from the bounded search.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
