night:P3K.12	2026-11-18T05:10:33.274105+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved Elliptic fixed curves through actual smooth finite-root descent Read and rederived the entire proof with the current Satriano and Floyd openings. At each rank-one double curve the actual source equation is z=xy and line-circle weights are(0,1,−1). Every finite point stabilizer preserves the two weight lines and has a faithful base character. Its diagonal characters satisfy b+c=1 modulo its order. A pseudoreflection with nontrivial elliptic tangent character would fix both normal lines and the base, contradicting faithfulness. The explicit averaging linearization has derivative identity; Satriano Cor1.8 and Prop2.2 therefore make the elliptic tangent character trivial for every point stabilizer of a smooth quotient. One-dimensional linearization and analytic continuation show its effective setwise action on the elliptic curve is free. The actual quotient curve is elliptic by unramified Riemann–Hurwitz, including permuted double-curve orbits and possible normal ramification. A prime avoiding the two descended nonzero normal weights makes this an entire fixed component of the prime subgroup. The invariant normal exponential chart proves that component assertion. Floyd Theorem4.4 at n=0 then contradicts its four mod-prime Betti classes inside a six-sphere of total Betti number2.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
