night:P4.27	2026-11-18	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved as stated The exact Hopf pole graph has r elliptic roots and v rational vertices after k blowups, so equality forces k=v and zero conductor-image Euler number. In the all-elliptic image case every rational pole contracts and no elliptic root does. The resolution-to-minimal-model and resolution-to-normalization maps then have exactly the same connected fibres; normalizing their graph image gives proper finite birational projections to normal surfaces, hence a holomorphic isomorphism of the normalization with the minimal Hopf surface. In the sole remaining graph count, the homomorphism from the Hopf group to Z has finite kernel and each elliptic-root map has infinite image by the actual universal-cover lift argument. Quotienting each elliptic vertex by the saturated image of its rank-one kernel gives a surjection to a graph of cyclic groups. Removing its unique trivial-edge cycle leaves a tree amalgam containing Z; restoring it yields a free product with Z containing F2, contradicting virtual abelianness. Thus the equality normalization is smooth minimal Hopf. Source proof and historical review records were available; this is a re-derivation, not a blind check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
