night:P4R.17	2026-11-18T05:10:56.410177+00:00	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved Full unrestricted delta-four nonplanar triple classification, exact ambient morphisms and all local bounds. For any normalized conormal lattice E, the exact sequence along the saturated Hessian line gives a+b=e1+e2. A unit Hessian column gives d≥a and E⊂t^e1K gives b≥e1, hence d/2+b≥e1+e2/2 without assuming f∈P². The nonplanar branch estimate gives delta+3+m/2. For three smooth branches and delta4, classified the entire finite-colength analytic ring from its first2 jets. One first-jet direction gives the exact common-tangent model with E=t²K on each branch, defect13. Two first-jet directions force two proportional branch evaluations; after actual parameter changes, the residual coupling mu≠0 gives two analytic generators and hence a planar ring. For mu=0 the exact contact-three-plus-line ideal has conormal orders(1,3),(1,3),(1,1), giving21/2. For multiplicity4, branch delta2 would leave the minimally glued ring of embedding dimension4; hence the singular branch is the ordinary cusp. The colength-one module makes m0²⊂A, and embedding dimension3 forces mA²=m0². Classified its cotangent hyperplane and product map. A nonzero cusp-cubic coefficient gives independent tangent axes; the only allowed initial cubic xyz has rank-two leading Hessian and therefore vanishes, giving f∈m4 and defect11. With zero cubic coefficient, the three other coefficients must all be nonzero; the actual model has ideal(z(x−y),xy(x−y),z²−x²y). Its Hilbert–Burch minors, generic reducedness and depth give exact equality with the curve ideal. Primitive conormal matrices have orders(3,3),(1,2),(1,2), so defect23/2. The delta3 and delta2 cases then follow from the explicitly rederived excess-one ring classification. The unchanged a3_delta4.py verifies all9 lattices and the4 exact jet identities; its received historical checker wording is not counted as a new check