night:P4R.6	2026-11-18	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, effort Pro, S6_10_PAPERS	targeted proof check	proved as stated Finite Gorenstein duality produces the effective horizontal conductor in the pulled meromorphic canonical divisor. The actual principal-function exceptional intersection equation proves negative definiteness and strict positivity of minus the inverse matrix on each block. Minimal-resolution adjunction gives nonnegative right-hand coefficients, so all exceptional pole coefficients are nonnegative. A zero block is a disjoint rational minus-two configuration outside the conductor. Its isolated hypersurface morsification supplies an embedded vanishing sphere of square minus two in a nearby torus via the normalized root cover, contradicting asphericity. Hence every exceptional block meets the conductor and has positive coefficients. Source proof and historical review records were available; this is a re-derivation, not a blind check.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
