cdp:st:A.1.1	2026-11-18	Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) at effort max, S6_10 intake	targeted proof check	Holds. Re-derived the injectivity of the conormal map for a reduced hypersurface (generic smoothness of each component, reducedness), the exact sequences 0->N*->K->T->0 and 0->K->V->Q->0, criterion (A.1), and H^0(V(x)A)=ker delta_A when H^0(N*(x)A)=H^0(Q(x)A)=0. Not checked here: the paper's reading that the two endpoint vanishings of CDP20 p.692 are those of N*(x)A and Q(x)A (CDP20 not reopened).		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
cdp:st:B1	2026-11-18	Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) at effort max, S6_10 intake	independent re-proof	Holds. Re-derived every entry of table (B.1): at the node, torsion C_node generated by v dw, torsion-free quotient nu_*O(-2), ambient kernel K=nu_*O (generators w dv, v dw, conormal dt=v dw+w dv); h^0=h^1=d_lambda for A_lambda; Kunneth on C_0 x P^1 gives (1,1+d,d) for the ambient and cotangent sheaves and (0,1+d,d) for the torsion-free quotient. The family y^2=x^3+x^2+t has smooth total space and singular fibres only at t=0,-4/27; A_lambda=O(P-Q) with descent scalar (1-a)/(1+a)=lambda for a=(1-lambda)/(1+lambda). So the conormal and torsion-free vanishings hold for lambda!=1 while h^0 of the ambient cotangent sheaf is 1 for every lambda.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
