night:P3K.68	2026-11-19	Claude Opus 5.5 at effort max, a6d42bf6fe2b0d8a8, intake of S6_06_BLIND cp12-cp36, gap 4 (second model family)	targeted proof check	holds as far as checked, with one input left: (1) by explicit quaternion arithmetic, q_H = c0 + j conj(c1) preserves orientation, the physical circle q -> q e^{-it} has weights (-1,+1) on (c0,c1) and acts by a common positive scalar on the spinor (conj c0, c1), [S^3_H] = -[S^1_delta][S^2_z], [P^1_right] = -[S^2_z] and [P(spinor)] = +[S^2_z]; so the line whose nonzero vectors carry the physical circle (the tautological line of the spinor) has Chern number -1 on the outward circle-first meridian, and the meridian-one Thom line is its dual U = M^-1 (PL.1, PL.2a). (2) Changing x to -x on the fixed oriented six-manifold negates k = int x^3 and l = int p1 x, so the choice is a global sign on every class off the reference fan and leaves every multiplicative rule unchanged. (3) PL.6 then uses the physical circle in the Hopf gluing of P3F.22 with that gluing's positive-generator orientation (S^2_z and S^3_y both reversed, six-dimensional orientation unchanged), which gives x_phys = c1(M) = -x_Thom and lambda_M(F) = -Sigma_{F^-1}; the orientation bookkeeping checks. Left unchecked: the normalization of P3F.22 itself (lambda(b) has mu = +1/28), which fixes the overall sign of every class in both conventions alike. Verdict: M is the right line relative to P3F.22. [Received locator: reviews/INTAKE_S6_06_BLIND_cp36_scripts/physical_line_orientation.py (.out); papers/IV/body.tex P3K.68 proof PL.1-PL.6]		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
