series:sweep:15	2026-11-19	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, reasoning effort inherited from root (not separately exposed), S6_SERIES_GRIND/corrections_audit	used and rechecked in this run	Sweep correction 15: The supplied night register has 299 rows at cp36, and cp15 paper text carries K113-K119. Missing P1.6/P1.14/P5.7 are explicitly identified; their preservation and integration instructions accompany this report. Action: Use cp36 as source identity; import the two reported classification checks and insert the credited P5.7 comparison. Scope: the stated correction only; this event does not certify the entire receiving proof.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
series:sweep:16	2026-11-19	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, reasoning effort inherited from root (not separately exposed), S6_SERIES_GRIND/corrections_audit	used and rechecked in this run	Sweep correction 16: No Q03 rows occur in the inherited S6 inventory and no dedicated Q03 deliverable is present in the attached tree. Sweep16 directs a separate tag space for its scheduling manuscript. Action: Record the editorial scope choice from sweep16. This asserts no absence of mathematical relations between the subjects and gives no proof check to the scheduling results. Scope: the stated correction only; this event does not certify the entire receiving proof.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
night:P3K.68	2026-11-19	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, reasoning effort inherited from root (not separately exposed), S6_SERIES_GRIND/corrections_audit	computation or formal certificate	Fresh independent_orientation_checks.py derives quaternion Hopf derivatives, Cox/projective determinant signs, exterior-form collar transgression, and global x -> -x characteristic transport without importing earlier code. All exact checks pass. This confirms the displayed arithmetic and orientation maps; it gives no substitute for primary-source verification of Jin coordinates.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
night:P3F.22	2026-11-19	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, reasoning effort inherited from root (not separately exposed), S6_SERIES_GRIND/corrections_audit	computation or formal certificate	Fresh independent_orientation_checks.py expands exp(z/2) A-hat in degree eight, eliminates p2 via the signature polynomial, computes the inverse intersection pairing for [[0,1],[1,k]], and obtains mu(lambda(f))=(4k-l)/672. At (k,l)=(8,8) this is +1/28, agreeing with the imported second-model derivation. Geometric realization, gluing direction and the given Jin coordinates are retained inputs.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
maps:src:F.4.1	2026-11-19	GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI), ChatGPT Pro mode, reasoning effort inherited from root (not separately exposed), S6_SERIES_GRIND/corrections_audit	independent re-proof	Classification implication independently written in fourfold_classification_prereading.md before reading the target proof. Given P1.12/P1.13, the diagonal cohomology isometry preserves q and p1 and hence the full normal clutching pair; Wall extended-form classification gives the oriented almost diffeomorphism, and Kramer-Stolz Theorem A absorbs the sphere in a positive HP2 summand. Source statements opened: Kramer-Stolz p178 and Conway-Crowley-Powell-Sixt Definition3.6/Theorem3.7. Construction and characteristic inputs are not independently re-proved by this event.		s6_pro_prompts_20261112_work/returns/S6_SERIES_GRIND_checkpoint_10_20261120T0211Z_unzipped/CHECK_EVENTS.tsv	
